;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; ==================================================================================================
;; Grecharged-mesh-browser — the debug MESH BROWSER (owner's direct request).
;;
;; WHY THIS EXISTS. The owner is the project's only reliable visual judge (standing rule: the agent
;; NEVER measures the in-game visual). Until now he could only judge the handful of surfaces he
;; happened to walk past, and six PBR rounds were spent on five hand-named surfaces. This browser
;; puts him in front of ANY of a level's meshes, worst-grade first, in real game conditions, with
;; the checker / displacement / relief / time-of-day all switchable while he looks — and it DISPLAYS
;; the offline test's grade so he can CONFIRM OR REFUTE the tool's verdict (the cross-check loop that
;; every previous round lacked).
;;
;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; REOPENED 2026-07-29 — owner: "C'est impossible a parcourir via le tactile (le mesh browser)"
;;
;; He has no gamepad permanently attached and no adb, so a browser that needs either is a browser he
;; cannot use. THREE independent defects made touch non-functional; all three are fixed here:
;;
;;  1. NO TOUCH EVENT EVER REACHED THE BROWSER. The Android overlay only forwards a tap
;;     (NativeGk.onMenuTap) when NativeGk.isInMenu() is true. isInMenu() is a native sniff of
;;     *master-mode* / *progress-process*, and the browser deliberately runs in master-mode 'game.
;;     So the tap path was dead by construction. FIX: the browser now raises a native flag
;;     (pc-mb-set-active!) that the overlay polls; while raised, the overlay suspends the virtual
;;     gamepad and forwards RAW multi-touch instead.
;;
;;  2. THE HIT-TEST WAS OFF BY 2x. Row hit-testing normalised the drawn y by 448.0, but the 2D draw
;;     space is screen-sy = 224 units tall (draw-sprite2d-xy clamps to screen-miny..screen-maxy,
;;     which span screen-sy; see engine/gfx/hw/video.gc set-video-mode). Every row was therefore
;;     hit-tested at half its true height, so a tap selected the wrong row or nothing at all. The
;;     observe button strip was worse: drawn at y=232..248 and x up to 1090, i.e. entirely outside
;;     the 512x224 design space — invisible AND unhittable, while its tap zones were spread across
;;     the whole screen. FIX: this file now defines its layout ONCE in normalised [0,1] coordinates
;;     and converts to draw units at the last moment, so the drawn rectangle and the tap target are
;;     the same rectangle by construction.
;;
;;  3. THERE WAS NO GESTURE DATA AT ALL. pc-get-touch-tap carries a single tap EDGE — no
;;     finger-down/up, no motion, no second finger. Swipe, drag, pinch and fling were not merely
;;     unbound, they had no source. A 3613-entry list (village1) stepped one row at a time is
;;     unusable by construction. FIX: a real gesture recogniser in game/kernel/jak1/kmachine.cpp
;;     (pc_mb_touch_event) fed by the overlay, polled once per frame here.
;;
;; The touch design is the one every phone user already knows: drag the list to scroll (with
;; inertia), drag the right-edge handle to cross thousands of rows in one gesture, tap a row to
;; select it, drag in the 3D view to orbit (horizontal = azimuth, vertical = elevation), pinch to
;; zoom, two-finger drag to spin the mesh, and a grid of finger-sized buttons for every toggle.
;; Nothing requires a gamepad; nothing requires adb.
;;
;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; REOPENED AGAIN 2026-07-29 — owner: "le warp to model warp toujours au meme endroit, et warp le
;; joueur... Moi je voulais pouvoir tourner en FREE CAM autour dudit mesh (origine au centre du
;; modele) pour pouvoir le voir sous toutes les coutures"
;;
;; Selecting a mesh no longer moves the player AT ALL. See the block above
;; mesh-browser-request-level for the full rationale; in one line: the camera goes to the mesh
;; centroid, Jak stays exactly where he was standing, and the level (not the player) is what gets
;; requested when the mesh lives somewhere else.
;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;;
;; ARCHITECTURE. A self-contained debug overlay, not a game-option array (a 3613-row dynamic list
;; does not fit that static-array framework). It is driven by ONE per-frame call,
;; (mesh-browser-update), hooked into (update *pc-settings*) right next to draw-pc-fps-counter — the
;; always-live per-frame path that renders on BOTH x86 (GL) and Android (GLES, no ImGui, no
;; debug-segment gate). It owns the screen only while active; when closed it does nothing and the
;; normal render path is byte-for-byte unchanged.
;;
;; OBSERVES, DOES NOT FIX. Nothing here changes a displacement/PBR shader law. The checker toggle
;; only re-points the EXISTING PbrTestPattern debug material (applied at the next level load, so a
;; flip re-warps the current mesh).
;; ==================================================================================================

;; ---- C++ back end (game/kernel/jak1/kmachine.cpp) --------------------------------------------------
;; The per-level catalogue distilled from tess_sign (tools/mesh_index) is parsed in C++ and shipped
;; INSIDE the APK next to the bundled recharged textures (owner rule: derived data goes in the APK).
(define-extern pc-mesh-index-load! (function string int))                 ;; parse level index -> count
(define-extern pc-mesh-index-count (function int))                        ;; loaded mesh count
(define-extern pc-mesh-index-geti (function int int int))                 ;; (row field) -> scalar
(define-extern pc-mesh-index-getf (function int int float))               ;; (row field) -> metres
(define-extern pc-mesh-index-name! (function int string symbol))          ;; material name -> string
(define-extern pc-mesh-index-level! (function string symbol))             ;; loaded level name -> string
(define-extern pc-set-mesh-browser-checker! (function int none))          ;; 0 real / 1 checker
(define-extern pc-mesh-browser-export! (function int none))               ;; write files/mesh_select.txt
;; REOPEN: the real gesture channel + the observable-state dump.
(define-extern pc-mb-set-active! (function int none))     ;; tell the Android overlay we own the screen
(define-extern pc-mb-touch-poll! (function int))          ;; latch a frame of gestures, consume deltas
(define-extern pc-mb-touch-geti (function int int))       ;; read a field of the latched frame
(define-extern pc-mb-state-begin! (function none))        ;; start files/mesh_browser_state.txt
(define-extern pc-mb-state-line! (function string none))  ;; append one line
(define-extern pc-mb-state-end! (function none))          ;; append touch counters + write the file
;; V2 FREECAM (owner 2026-07-30: "le mesh browser actuel est a chier" — the reticle-first freecam
;; below is the primary UI now; the list survives as the secondary way in). These bridges live in
;; game/kernel/jak1/kmachine.cpp next to the pc-mb-touch channel.
(define-extern pc-mb-pick-levels! (function string string none)) ;; up to 2 ACTIVE level index-names to pick against ("" = unused slot)
(define-extern pc-mb-pick! (function vector vector int))   ;; camera ray origin+dir (GOAL units); slab-tests every index row AABB, near->far, cap 16; returns count. ALSO arms the render-thread TRIANGLE ray-test (v2.1)
(define-extern pc-mb-pick-ready? (function int))           ;; v2.1: 1 once the renderers' triangle results are folded in (list re-sorted by REAL surface distance); 0 while pending
(define-extern pc-mb-pick-geti (function int int int))     ;; (idx field): 0=row 1=slot 2=t_cm
(define-extern pc-mb-target-set! (function int int none))  ;; (row slot) -> renderer target key; ALSO clears hide/checker/gizmo flags C++-side
(define-extern pc-mb-target-clear! (function none))
(define-extern pc-mb-hide-set! (function int none))
(define-extern pc-mb-checker-set! (function int none))
(define-extern pc-mb-gizmos-set! (function int none))
(define-extern pc-mb-rt-geti (function int int))           ;; render-thread proof counters: 0 hidden_draws 1 checker_draws 2 gizmo_draws 3 gizmo_faces (monotonic); v2.3: 11 wireframe edges last frame 12 hovered tri ordinal (-1 none) 13 ACTIVE marks; v2.4: 14 marked tris drawn last frame (== 13 while browser open) 15 gizmo occlusion-query samples passed last frame
;; V2.3 reticle forensics (registered next to the pc-mb-* channel in game/kernel/jak1/kmachine.cpp)
(define-extern pc-mb-hover-ray! (function vector vector int none)) ;; publish the reticle ray (origin GOAL units, dir any length) to the render thread; on=1 highlights the hovered polygon while gizmos are up, on=0 disarms
(define-extern pc-mb-mark-poly! (function int))            ;; TOGGLE the hovered polygon's mark: append it as JSONL to mesh_marks.jsonl (external asset root) + persistent orange highlight, or (v2.4) UNMARK an already-marked polygon (highlight AND its JSONL line removed); returns the ACTIVE mark count, -1 = no hovered polygon / no target

;; pc-mb-pick-geti field ids
(defconstant MB_PK_ROW 0)
(defconstant MB_PK_SLOT 1)
(defconstant MB_PK_TCM 2)

;; geti field ids
(defconstant MB_GI_SYSTEM 0)    ;; 0 TFRAG, 1 TIE
(defconstant MB_GI_GRADED 1)    ;; 1 if the sign test graded this mesh
(defconstant MB_GI_ASIGN 2)     ;; A_sign percent x100, -1 ungraded
(defconstant MB_GI_BDISP 3)     ;; B_disp percent x100, -1 n/a
(defconstant MB_GI_TEX 4)
(defconstant MB_GI_SHELL 5)
;; getf field ids (metres)
(defconstant MB_GF_CX 0)
(defconstant MB_GF_CY 1)
(defconstant MB_GF_CZ 2)
(defconstant MB_GF_LOX 3)
(defconstant MB_GF_LOY 4)
(defconstant MB_GF_LOZ 5)
(defconstant MB_GF_HIX 6)
(defconstant MB_GF_HIY 7)
(defconstant MB_GF_HIZ 8)

;; gesture field ids — mirror pc_mb_touch_geti in game/kernel/jak1/kmachine.cpp
(defconstant MB_T_FINGERS 0)
(defconstant MB_T_X 1)
(defconstant MB_T_Y 2)
(defconstant MB_T_DX 3)         ;; drag delta since the last poll, consumed once
(defconstant MB_T_DY 4)
(defconstant MB_T_PINCH 5)      ;; change in two-finger separation
(defconstant MB_T_D2X 6)        ;; two-finger centroid travel
(defconstant MB_T_D2Y 7)
(defconstant MB_T_TAPSEQ 8)     ;; monotonic: a tap happened
(defconstant MB_T_TAPX 9)
(defconstant MB_T_TAPY 10)
(defconstant MB_T_UPSEQ 11)     ;; monotonic: a gesture ended
(defconstant MB_T_FLING 12)     ;; release velocity for inertia (screen-fractions/s x10000)
(defconstant MB_T_DOWNSEQ 13)   ;; monotonic: a gesture started
(defconstant MB_T_DOWNX 14)
(defconstant MB_T_DOWNY 15)
(defconstant MB_T_NEVENTS 16)   ;; total raw touch events seen (evidence counter)

;; ---- state ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The browser has five top-level modes: closed, the LEVEL picker, the MESH LIST, OBSERVE, and the
;; V2 FREECAM — a camera fully detached from Jak, flown with the sticks, that targets whatever mesh
;; sits under a first-person reticle.
(defenum mesh-browser-mode
  :type int32
  (closed 0)
  (levels 1)
  (list 2)
  (observe 3)
  (freecam 4))

;; A level entry: the on-disk index file name and the LEVEL SYMBOL.
;; The symbol is what the load-state wants (load-state-want-levels); there is no continue-point name
;; any more, because the browser no longer respawns the player anywhere.
(deftype mesh-browser-level (structure)
  ((index-name string)     ;; mesh_index_<index-name>.txt
   (sym        symbol)))   ;; the engine's level symbol (engine/level/level-info.gc :name)

;; The list FILTERS the owner asked for.
(defenum mesh-browser-filter
  :type int32
  (all 0)          ;; every mesh
  (failing 1)      ;; only meshes the offline test graded < 100%
  (tfrag 2)        ;; only TFRAG (the tessellation system — where B_disp is meaningful)
  (tie 3))         ;; only TIE (per-pixel POM)

;; What the current finger-drag is doing. Latched at touch-down from WHERE the finger landed, and
;; held for the whole gesture — so a drag that starts on the list never turns into an orbit halfway.
(defenum mesh-browser-drag
  :type int32
  (none 0)
  (scroll 1)       ;; dragging the list body
  (handle 2)       ;; dragging the right-edge fast-scroll handle
  (orbit 3))       ;; dragging in the 3D view

(deftype mesh-browser (basic)
  ((mode          mesh-browser-mode)
   ;; level picker
   (level-index   int32)
   ;; mesh list
   (filter        mesh-browser-filter)
   (n-total       int32)          ;; raw index rows for the loaded level
   (sel           int32)          ;; selected row INTO the filtered view
   (scroll-f      float)          ;; first visible filtered row, fractional (smooth scrolling)
   (scroll-vel    float)          ;; inertia, rows per frame
   (n-filtered    int32)          ;; count passing the filter
   (view          (array int32))  ;; filtered->raw row map (index-sorted worst-first already)
   ;; gesture bookkeeping
   (drag          mesh-browser-drag)
   ;; the selected mesh (raw row), cached for OBSERVE
   (cur-row       int32)
   ;; observation state — the browser owns the camera outright in OBSERVE (see
   ;; mesh-browser-place-camera), so orbit/elevation/zoom are exactly these three numbers.
   (obs-focus     vector :inline) ;; world centroid (GOAL units) we warped to
   (obs-az        float)          ;; camera azimuth around the mesh, radians
   (obs-el        float)          ;; camera elevation, radians, clamped away from the poles
   (obs-dist      float)          ;; camera distance (GOAL units)
   (frame-dist    float)          ;; auto-frame distance from the bbox (GOAL units)
   (spin          float)          ;; MESH spin: camera AND light rotate together about the centroid
   (checker?      symbol)         ;; real-texture <-> checker toggle
   (need-reframe  symbol)         ;; recompute the framing once the level is up
   (warp-timer    int32)          ;; frames since the request, to let the level load before framing
   ;; FREE-CAMERA bookkeeping (owner 2026-07-29: "je voulais pouvoir tourner en free cam autour
   ;; dudit mesh (origine au centre du modele)"). The browser moves the CAMERA and nothing else, so
   ;; it has to remember the world it borrowed and hand it back untouched on close.
   (browse-level  symbol)         ;; level whose mesh we are looking at
   (home-level    symbol)         ;; the level the PLAYER is standing in — never unloaded from under him
   (home-pos      vector :inline) ;; where the player was when the browser opened, to PROVE he never moved
   (frozen?       symbol)         ;; we put the player process to sleep (he must not wander off-screen)
   (saved-border? symbol)         ;; setting-control border-mode as we found it
   ;; the load-state want list exactly as we found it, so close puts the world back
   (saved-want0   symbol) (saved-want1 symbol)
   (saved-disp0   symbol) (saved-disp1 symbol)
   (reload-timer  int32)          ;; checker flip: re-request the level so its textures re-upload
   ;; state-dump throttle
   (dump-sig      int32)
   (dump-timer    int32)
   ;; ---- V2 FREECAM (owner 2026-07-30 redesign) ----------------------------------------------------
   ;; The freecam is its own camera pose (position + yaw/pitch, radians), not an orbit: the owner
   ;; flies it anywhere, including the air, and targets meshes through the reticle instead of a list.
   (fc-pos         vector :inline) ;; camera position, GOAL units
   (fc-yaw         float)          ;; look yaw, radians, kept in [0,2pi)
   (fc-pitch       float)          ;; look pitch, radians, clamped short of the poles (MB_EL_MIN/MAX)
   (fc-target      int32)          ;; targeted index row, -1 = none
   (fc-target-slot int32)          ;; which pick-level slot the target's row belongs to (0/1)
   (fc-pick-n      int32)          ;; candidate count from the last reticle pick
   ;; V2.1 async pick: R1/R2 fires the request; the render thread ray-tests the candidates'
   ;; REAL triangles over the next frame; the poll below completes the pick once ready (or
   ;; after a timeout, falling back to the AABB order — nothing rendering = nothing pickable).
   (fc-pick-wait   int32)          ;; 0 = idle; >0 = frames spent waiting on pc-mb-pick-ready?
   (fc-pick-dir    int32)          ;; +1 (R1) / -1 (R2) of the pending request
   (fc-marks       int32)          ;; V2.3: session total of pc-mb-mark-poly! JSONL marks (default 0)
   (fc-hide?       symbol)         ;; GOAL-side mirror of the C++ hide flag (C++ is authoritative)
   (fc-checker?    symbol)         ;; ditto, per-target checker tessellation
   (fc-gizmos?     symbol)         ;; ditto, normal gizmos
   (fc-lvl0        string)         ;; the up-to-2 ACTIVE level index-names the picker tests against
   (fc-lvl1        string)
   ;; scratch strings (runtime buffers, re-formatted each frame — like *fps-counter-label*).
   ;; grade-buf / sub-buf hold pre-formatted sub-strings so they can be passed as ~S args to an
   ;; OUTER string-format WITHOUT clobber: string-format formats into the SINGLE shared *temp-string*
   ;; and reads its args AFTER, so a nested string-format (or mb-grade-string, which uses one) as an
   ;; arg would be overwritten. These dedicated buffers keep each sub-string alive across that read.
   (name-buf      string)
   (level-buf     string)
   (line-buf      string)
   (grade-buf     string)
   (sub-buf       string))
  (:methods
   (mesh-browser-open (_type_) none)
   (mesh-browser-close (_type_) none)
   (mesh-browser-rebuild-view (_type_) none)
   (mesh-browser-observe-selected (_type_) none)))

(define *mesh-browser* (new 'global 'mesh-browser))
;; V2.3: explicit one-time init — the mark total is a SESSION counter, so it must not be reset on
;; every freecam entry, only here.
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* fc-marks) 0)

;; EVERY level that has a shipped mesh_index_*.txt — all 25 of them (owner's delivery condition:
;; "faudrait que le navigateur soit inclus avec les corrections de tous les mesh pour que ce soit
;; pertinent que je puisse TOUT previsualiser"). index-name matches tools/mesh_index output, sym is
;; the engine level symbol from engine/level/level-info.gc. Order = the hub/story order, with the
;; non-story levels after it.
(define *mesh-browser-levels*
  (new 'static 'boxed-array :type mesh-browser-level
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "village1"   :sym 'village1)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "beach"      :sym 'beach)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "jungle"     :sym 'jungle)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "jungleb"    :sym 'jungleb)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "misty"      :sym 'misty)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "firecanyon" :sym 'firecanyon)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "village2"   :sym 'village2)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "sunken"     :sym 'sunken)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "sunkenb"    :sym 'sunkenb)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "swamp"      :sym 'swamp)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "rolling"    :sym 'rolling)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "ogre"       :sym 'ogre)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "village3"   :sym 'village3)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "snow"       :sym 'snow)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "maincave"   :sym 'maincave)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "darkcave"   :sym 'darkcave)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "robocave"   :sym 'robocave)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "lavatube"   :sym 'lavatube)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "citadel"    :sym 'citadel)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "finalboss"  :sym 'finalboss)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "training"   :sym 'training)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "test-zone"  :sym 'test-zone)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "intro"      :sym 'intro)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "demo"       :sym 'demo)
    (new 'static 'mesh-browser-level :index-name "title"      :sym 'title)))

;; view backing store (max index we can hold; village1 is 3613)
;; Sized to the LARGEST shipped index (lavatube, 19490 rows), measured over all 25 mesh_index files.
;; The previous 8192 silently dropped more than half of lavatube and a third of village1 from the
;; list — "tout previsualiser" forbids a silent cap. 20480 x int32 = 80 KB, allocated once.
(defconstant MB_MAX_MESHES 20480)
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* view) (new 'global 'boxed-array int32 MB_MAX_MESHES))
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* name-buf)  (new 'global 'string 64 (the string #f)))
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* level-buf) (new 'global 'string 64 (the string #f)))
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* line-buf)  (new 'global 'string 192 (the string #f)))
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* grade-buf) (new 'global 'string 16 (the string #f)))
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* sub-buf)   (new 'global 'string 16 (the string #f)))
;; freecam pick-level name buffers — longest level name is "firecanyon" (10), 32 is comfortable.
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* fc-lvl0)   (new 'global 'string 32 (the string #f)))
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* fc-lvl1)   (new 'global 'string 32 (the string #f)))
;; (new 'global 'string n #f) allocates without writing a terminator (kernel/gstring.gc:70), and
;; level-buf is printed with ~S from the very first LEVELS frame, before enter-list fills it.
(clear (-> *mesh-browser* level-buf))
(clear (-> *mesh-browser* name-buf))
(clear (-> *mesh-browser* line-buf))
(clear (-> *mesh-browser* grade-buf))
(clear (-> *mesh-browser* sub-buf))
(clear (-> *mesh-browser* fc-lvl0))
(clear (-> *mesh-browser* fc-lvl1))
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* checker?) #f)
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* fc-target) -1)
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* fc-hide?) #f)
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* fc-checker?) #f)
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* fc-gizmos?) #f)
(set! (-> *mesh-browser* mode) (mesh-browser-mode closed))

;; ---- the 2D design space --------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; draw-sprite2d-xy clamps x into 1792..2304 and y into screen-miny..screen-maxy, i.e. 512 units wide
;; by screen-sy (=224 NTSC / 256 PAL) tall; draw-string-xy shares that space once the caller has
;; pre-multiplied y by relative-y-scale (see draw-pc-fps-counter, which does exactly that). Designing
;; against a fixed 512x224 grid and letting mb-yscale carry the PAL stretch makes the mapping exact:
;;   normalized_y = design_y / 224   and   normalized_x = design_x / 512
;; independently of video mode. EVERY rectangle below is declared in normalized [0,1] coordinates and
;; converted here, so the rectangle that is DRAWN and the rectangle that is HIT-TESTED are the same
;; rectangle. The pre-reopen code kept two hand-written copies of that arithmetic and they disagreed.
(defconstant MB_DX 512.0)
(defconstant MB_DY 224.0)

;; GOAL world units -> metres (1 metre = 4096 units). Used only by the state dump, so every number
;; the owner or a device test reads back is in the same unit as the index's centroids.
(defconstant MB_M 0.000244140625)

(defmacro mb-yscale (y)
  `(the int (* ,y (-> (get-video-params) relative-y-scale))))

(defun mb-px ((nx float))
  "Normalized x -> design x."
  (the int (* nx MB_DX)))

(defun mb-py ((ny float))
  "Normalized y -> design y."
  (the int (* ny MB_DY)))

;; ---- list geometry, in normalized coordinates -----------------------------------------------------
(defconstant MB_PAGE 14)          ;; rows per page (bigger rows = finger-sized targets on a phone)
(defconstant MB_LIST_TOP 0.175)
(defconstant MB_LIST_BOT 0.900)
(defconstant MB_TRACK_X0 0.945)   ;; fast-scroll handle track (right edge)
(defconstant MB_BTN_TOP 0.020)    ;; header button row
(defconstant MB_BTN_BOT 0.115)
(defconstant MB_FOOT_TOP 0.910)
(defconstant MB_FOOT_BOT 0.990)

(defmacro mb-row-h ()
  `(/ (- MB_LIST_BOT MB_LIST_TOP) (the float MB_PAGE)))

;; rows spanned by one unit of normalized vertical finger travel
(defmacro mb-rows-per-unit ()
  `(/ (the float MB_PAGE) (- MB_LIST_BOT MB_LIST_TOP)))

;; ---- drawing helpers ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defun mesh-browser-text ((buf dma-buffer) (str string) (nx float) (ny float) (col font-color))
  "One HUD text line, positioned in normalized coordinates."
  (draw-string-xy str buf (mb-px nx) (mb-yscale (the float (mb-py ny))) col (font-flags shadow kerning))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-rect ((buf dma-buffer) (x0 float) (y0 float) (x1 float) (y1 float) (col rgba))
  "One translucent panel / row highlight / button, in normalized coordinates."
  (draw-sprite2d-xy buf
                    (mb-px x0)
                    (mb-yscale (the float (mb-py y0)))
                    (- (mb-px x1) (mb-px x0))
                    (- (mb-yscale (the float (mb-py y1))) (mb-yscale (the float (mb-py y0))))
                    col)
  (none))

;; ---- the gesture channel ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; One latch per frame; every screen then reads the SAME snapshot. The deltas are consumed by the
;; latch, so no screen can double-apply them.

(deftype mb-gest (structure)
  ((fingers  int32)
   (x        float) (y     float)   ;; live position of the primary finger, normalized
   (dx       float) (dy    float)   ;; travel since the last frame
   (pinch    float)                 ;; change in two-finger separation
   (d2x      float) (d2y   float)   ;; two-finger centroid travel
   (fling    float)                 ;; release velocity, screen-fractions/second
   (tap?     symbol) (tap-x float) (tap-y float)
   (down?    symbol) (down-x float) (down-y float)
   (up?      symbol)
   (n-events int32)
   ;; previous monotonic counters, to turn them into per-frame edges
   (last-tap int32) (last-down int32) (last-up int32)))
(define *mb-gest* (new 'global 'mb-gest))

(defmacro mb-q (field)
  "Read a 0..10000 fixed-point gesture field as a normalized float."
  `(* 0.0001 (the float (pc-mb-touch-geti ,field))))

(defun mesh-browser-poll-touch ()
  "Latch this frame's gestures. On desktop (no touch source) every field stays 0 and every gesture
   test below is simply false, so the gamepad path is unaffected."
  (pc-mb-touch-poll!)
  (let ((g *mb-gest*))
    (set! (-> g fingers) (pc-mb-touch-geti MB_T_FINGERS))
    (set! (-> g x) (mb-q MB_T_X))
    (set! (-> g y) (mb-q MB_T_Y))
    (set! (-> g dx) (mb-q MB_T_DX))
    (set! (-> g dy) (mb-q MB_T_DY))
    (set! (-> g pinch) (mb-q MB_T_PINCH))
    (set! (-> g d2x) (mb-q MB_T_D2X))
    (set! (-> g d2y) (mb-q MB_T_D2Y))
    (set! (-> g fling) (mb-q MB_T_FLING))
    (set! (-> g n-events) (pc-mb-touch-geti MB_T_NEVENTS))
    ;; monotonic counters -> single-frame edges
    (let ((ts (pc-mb-touch-geti MB_T_TAPSEQ)))
      (set! (-> g tap?) (if (!= ts (-> g last-tap)) #t #f))
      (set! (-> g last-tap) ts))
    (let ((ds (pc-mb-touch-geti MB_T_DOWNSEQ)))
      (set! (-> g down?) (if (!= ds (-> g last-down)) #t #f))
      (set! (-> g last-down) ds))
    (let ((us (pc-mb-touch-geti MB_T_UPSEQ)))
      (set! (-> g up?) (if (!= us (-> g last-up)) #t #f))
      (set! (-> g last-up) us))
    (set! (-> g tap-x) (mb-q MB_T_TAPX))
    (set! (-> g tap-y) (mb-q MB_T_TAPY))
    (set! (-> g down-x) (mb-q MB_T_DOWNX))
    (set! (-> g down-y) (mb-q MB_T_DOWNY)))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-sync-touch ()
  "Re-baseline the monotonic counters without firing an edge — called when the browser opens so a
   stale tap from before it opened cannot select something on the first frame."
  (pc-mb-touch-poll!)
  (let ((g *mb-gest*))
    (set! (-> g last-tap) (pc-mb-touch-geti MB_T_TAPSEQ))
    (set! (-> g last-down) (pc-mb-touch-geti MB_T_DOWNSEQ))
    (set! (-> g last-up) (pc-mb-touch-geti MB_T_UPSEQ))
    (set! (-> g tap?) #f)
    (set! (-> g down?) #f)
    (set! (-> g up?) #f))
  (none))

(defun mb-in? ((px float) (py float) (x0 float) (y0 float) (x1 float) (y1 float))
  "Is a normalized point inside a normalized rect?"
  (and (>= px x0) (<= px x1) (>= py y0) (<= py y1)))

(defun mb-tap-in? ((x0 float) (y0 float) (x1 float) (y1 float))
  "Did this frame's TAP land in the rect? A tap only fires when the finger stayed still and lifted
   quickly, so a scroll-drag can never also select a row."
  (and (-> *mb-gest* tap?)
       (mb-in? (-> *mb-gest* tap-x) (-> *mb-gest* tap-y) x0 y0 x1 y1)))

(defun mb-down-in? ((x0 float) (y0 float) (x1 float) (y1 float))
  "Did this frame's finger-DOWN land in the rect? Used to latch what a drag will do."
  (and (-> *mb-gest* down?)
       (mb-in? (-> *mb-gest* down-x) (-> *mb-gest* down-y) x0 y0 x1 y1)))

(defun mb-button ((buf dma-buffer) (x0 float) (y0 float) (x1 float) (y1 float) (label string) (on? symbol))
  "Draw one finger-sized button and its label. The SAME rect is what mb-tap-in? tests."
  (mesh-browser-rect buf x0 y0 x1 y1
                     (if on?
                         (new 'static 'rgba :r #x40 :g #x80 :b #xd0 :a #xc0)
                         (new 'static 'rgba :r #x20 :g #x28 :b #x44 :a #xb0)))
  (mesh-browser-text buf label (+ x0 0.012) (+ y0 (* 0.62 (- y1 y0))) (font-color white))
  (none))

(defun mb-wrap ((v float) (hi float))
  "Wrap v into [0,hi) — used for stepping the hour (0..24) and angles (0..2pi). Steps are small so a
   single add/sub of hi suffices (no fmod in GOAL)."
  (cond
    ((< v 0.0) (+ v hi))
    ((>= v hi) (- v hi))
    (else v)))

(defun mb-pi-wrap ((v float))
  "Fold an angle into [-pi, pi] for sin-rad / cos-rad.

   THIS IS NOT COSMETIC. sin-rad and cos-rad (engine/math/trigonometry.gc:178 and :285) do NO range
   reduction — their own docstrings say 'No unwrap is done, should be in -pi, pi' — and outside that
   window the bare polynomial diverges instead of repeating: sin-rad(2pi) returns about +6.0, not 0.
   The orbit azimuth lives in [0, 2pi) and the mesh spin adds another full turn on top, so feeding it
   raw meant the camera flew off the orbit sphere over half of every 360-degree drag. That bug was
   live in the shipped browser and is a plausible part of what the owner saw."
  (let ((r v))
    (while (> r 3.14159274) (set! r (- r 6.28318548)))
    (while (< r -3.14159274) (set! r (+ r 6.28318548)))
    r))

(defun mesh-browser-active? ()
  "Is the browser currently owning the screen?"
  (!= (-> *mesh-browser* mode) (mesh-browser-mode closed)))

(defun mb-filter-name ((f mesh-browser-filter))
  (case f
    (((mesh-browser-filter all)) "ALL")
    (((mesh-browser-filter failing)) "FAILING")
    (((mesh-browser-filter tfrag)) "TFRAG")
    (((mesh-browser-filter tie)) "TIE")
    (else "?")))

(defun mb-grade-string ((obj mesh-browser) (raw int))
  "Format a mesh's offline grade into the browser's OWN grade-buf (n/a for ungraded TIE POM meshes).
   Uses the low-level (format (clear ...)) rather than the string-format macro so the result lives in
   grade-buf, not the shared *temp-string* — this is safe to pass as a ~S arg to an outer
   string-format (which would otherwise clobber a nested string-format's *temp-string*)."
  (if (= (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_GRADED) 1)
      (format (clear (-> obj grade-buf)) "~f%" (* 0.01 (the float (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_ASIGN))))
      (format (clear (-> obj grade-buf)) "n/a"))
  ;; return the buffer explicitly (do not rely on _format's return), like the string-format macro.
  (-> obj grade-buf))

(defun mesh-browser-scroll-max ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Largest legal first-visible row."
  (the float (max 0 (- (-> obj n-filtered) MB_PAGE))))

(defun mesh-browser-clamp-scroll ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Hold the list inside its bounds and kill the inertia at either end (no rubber-band: on a list of
   3613 rows a bounce just costs the owner another gesture)."
  (let ((hi (mesh-browser-scroll-max obj)))
    (when (< (-> obj scroll-f) 0.0)
      (set! (-> obj scroll-f) 0.0)
      (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0))
    (when (> (-> obj scroll-f) hi)
      (set! (-> obj scroll-f) hi)
      (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0)))
  (none))

;; ---- SHARED SCROLLING ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Used by BOTH pageable screens (the 25-level picker and the 3613-row mesh list), so the two can
;; never drift apart in feel. village1 alone holds 3613 rows: stepping that one row at a time is
;; unusable by construction, which is exactly what the owner hit.

(defun mesh-browser-list-scroll-physics ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Swipe / fast-scroll / inertia. Kept apart from the hit-testing so the scroll model is readable:
   while a finger is down the list tracks it exactly; when it lifts, the release velocity carries on
   and decays. Nothing here can select a row — selection is a TAP, which only fires when the finger
   did not travel."
  (let ((g *mb-gest*))
    ;; latch what this gesture is, from where the finger landed
    (when (-> g down?)
      (cond
        ((mb-down-in? MB_TRACK_X0 MB_LIST_TOP 1.0 MB_LIST_BOT)
         (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag handle))
         (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0))
        ((mb-down-in? 0.0 MB_LIST_TOP MB_TRACK_X0 MB_LIST_BOT)
         (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag scroll))
         (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0))  ;; touching the list stops a running fling, as expected
        (else (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none)))))
    (cond
      ;; dragging the fast-scroll handle: absolute position across the WHOLE filtered list
      ((and (= (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag handle)) (> (-> g fingers) 0))
       (let* ((span (- MB_LIST_BOT MB_LIST_TOP))
              (t0 (fmin 1.0 (fmax 0.0 (/ (- (-> g y) MB_LIST_TOP) span)))))
         (set! (-> obj scroll-f) (* t0 (mesh-browser-scroll-max obj)))))
      ;; dragging the list body: content follows the finger 1:1
      ((and (= (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag scroll)) (> (-> g fingers) 0))
       (set! (-> obj scroll-f) (- (-> obj scroll-f) (* (-> g dy) (mb-rows-per-unit)))))
      ;; no finger: inertia
      (else
       (when (!= (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0)
         (set! (-> obj scroll-f) (+ (-> obj scroll-f) (-> obj scroll-vel)))
         (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) (* (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.95))
         (when (< (fabs (-> obj scroll-vel)) 0.02) (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0)))))
    ;; release: a body drag hands its velocity to the inertia (rows/frame, 60 fps)
    (when (-> g up?)
      (when (= (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag scroll))
        (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) (* -0.0166 (* (-> g fling) (mb-rows-per-unit)))))
      (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none)))
    (mesh-browser-clamp-scroll obj))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-list-keep-sel-visible ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Only the GAMEPAD moves the selection blind, so only the gamepad needs the page to chase it. A
   touch scroll deliberately leaves the selection where it is."
  (let ((s (the float (-> obj sel))))
    (when (< s (-> obj scroll-f)) (set! (-> obj scroll-f) s))
    (when (> s (+ (-> obj scroll-f) (the float (- MB_PAGE 1))))
      (set! (-> obj scroll-f) (- s (the float (- MB_PAGE 1))))))
  (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0)
  (mesh-browser-clamp-scroll obj)
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-draw-scrollbar ((obj mesh-browser) (buf dma-buffer))
  "The right-edge track + handle. Dragging it crosses the whole list in ONE gesture, which is the
   only practical way through thousands of rows on a phone."
  (mesh-browser-rect buf MB_TRACK_X0 MB_LIST_TOP 0.998 MB_LIST_BOT
                     (new 'static 'rgba :r #x18 :g #x1c :b #x28 :a #xa0))
  (let* ((span (- MB_LIST_BOT MB_LIST_TOP))
         (n (max 1 (-> obj n-filtered)))
         (frac (fmin 1.0 (/ (the float MB_PAGE) (the float n))))
         (hh (fmax 0.045 (* span frac)))
         (hi (mesh-browser-scroll-max obj))
         (t0 (if (> hi 0.0) (fmin 1.0 (fmax 0.0 (/ (-> obj scroll-f) hi))) 0.0))
         (hy (+ MB_LIST_TOP (* t0 (- span hh)))))
    (mesh-browser-rect buf MB_TRACK_X0 hy 0.998 (+ hy hh)
                       (new 'static 'rgba :r #x60 :g #xa0 :b #xe0 :a #xd0)))
  (none))

(defmethod mesh-browser-rebuild-view mesh-browser ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Rebuild the filtered/sorted view for the loaded level index. The C++ index is ALREADY sorted
   worst-grade-first (ascending A_sign, then ascending B_disp, then bigger mesh first), so the view
   is just the subset passing the current filter, in the same order — worst first, no re-sort."
  (let ((n (pc-mesh-index-count))
        (m 0))
    (set! (-> obj n-total) n)
    (dotimes (i n)
      (when (< m MB_MAX_MESHES)
        (let* ((sys (pc-mesh-index-geti i MB_GI_SYSTEM))
               (graded (pc-mesh-index-geti i MB_GI_GRADED))
               (asign (pc-mesh-index-geti i MB_GI_ASIGN))
               (keep
                (case (-> obj filter)
                  (((mesh-browser-filter all)) #t)
                  ;; failing = graded AND below 100% (10000 = 100.00%)
                  (((mesh-browser-filter failing)) (and (= graded 1) (< asign 10000)))
                  (((mesh-browser-filter tfrag)) (= sys 0))
                  (((mesh-browser-filter tie)) (= sys 1))
                  (else #t))))
          (when keep
            (set! (-> obj view m) i)
            (+! m 1)))))
    (set! (-> obj n-filtered) m)
    (when (>= (-> obj sel) m) (set! (-> obj sel) (max 0 (+ m -1))))
    (when (< (-> obj sel) 0) (set! (-> obj sel) 0))
    (set! (-> obj scroll-f) 0.0)
    (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-cycle-filter ((obj mesh-browser) (f mesh-browser-filter))
  (set! (-> obj filter) f)
  (set! (-> obj sel) 0)
  (mesh-browser-rebuild-view obj)
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-enter-list ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Load the selected level's index and show the mesh list."
  (let ((lvl (-> *mesh-browser-levels* (-> obj level-index))))
    (pc-mesh-index-load! (-> lvl index-name))
    (pc-mesh-index-level! (-> obj level-buf)))
  (set! (-> obj filter) (mesh-browser-filter all))
  (set! (-> obj sel) 0)
  (mesh-browser-rebuild-view obj)
  (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none))
  (set! (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode list))
  (none))

;; ---- THE FREE CAMERA: borrow the world, move the CAMERA, hand the world back ----------------------
;; Owner, 2026-07-29: "J'ai l'impression que le warp to model warp toujours au meme endroit, et warp
;; le joueur, mais meme pas au bon endroit du coup... Moi je voulais pouvoir tourner en free cam
;; autour dudit mesh (origine au centre du modele) pour pouvoir le voir sous toutes les coutures".
;;
;; He was right twice over. The old code set *game-info* current-continue and called
;; (initialize! *game-info* 'die ...), which RESPAWNS Jak at the level's single fixed continue point
;; — literally "toujours au meme endroit", one spot per level, nowhere near the mesh — and then
;; pinned him to the centroid every frame. And walking is the wrong instrument anyway: you cannot
;; walk around a roof, a cornice, or the underside of an overhang, and those are exactly the
;; surfaces that carry the defects he has to inspect.
;;
;; What replaces it: THE PLAYER IS NEVER MOVED. Selecting a mesh only
;;   (a) asks the load-state for the mesh's level if it is not already active — the ordinary
;;       streaming mechanism (load-state-want-levels), not a continue point, and
;;   (b) puts the CAMERA on an orbit sphere centred on that mesh's CENTROID.
;; This is sound because background visibility is driven by the CAMERA, not by the player:
;; update-visible feeds (-> *math-camera* trans) into bsp-camera-asm
;; (engine/camera/cam-update.gc:84-97), so geometry 300 m away from Jak draws normally.
;; The player is only put to SLEEP, so he cannot wander, fall or die off-screen while the owner
;; looks; sleeping does not move him. Everything borrowed is handed back in mesh-browser-close.

(defun mesh-browser-frame-mesh ((obj mesh-browser))
  "AUTO-FRAMING: distance straight from the BOUNDING BOX, at a three-quarter viewing angle. Defined
   here rather than with the rest of OBSERVE because mesh-browser-observe-selected frames the mesh
   the instant it is picked, and GOAL needs the definition first."
  (set! (-> obj obs-az) 0.6)
  (set! (-> obj obs-el) 0.45)
  (set! (-> obj obs-dist) (-> obj frame-dist))
  (set! (-> obj spin) 0.0)
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-request-level ((obj mesh-browser) (sym symbol))
  "Make sure the mesh's level is up and visible, WITHOUT touching the player. Jak's own level is kept
   in the second want slot so the ground under him is never discarded — (update! *load-state*) drops
   any loaded level that is not named in the want list (engine/level/level.gc:1088)."
  (when sym
    (set! (-> obj browse-level) sym)
    (if (and (-> obj home-level) (!= (-> obj home-level) sym))
        (load-state-want-levels sym (-> obj home-level))
        (load-state-want-levels sym (the symbol #f)))
    ;; 'display-no-wait, NOT 'display. With plain 'display, (update! *load-state*) sends the player
    ;; an event while the level streams — engine/level/level.gc:1143-1144 does
    ;; (send-event *target* 'loading) — and target-handler.gc answers it with (go target-load-wait),
    ;; which plays a trip-and-fall. send-event is delivered synchronously, so the sleep bit does not
    ;; stop it: the player would be left mid-stumble the moment the browser closed. That is exactly
    ;; the "it moves Jak" complaint, by another route.
    (load-state-want-display-level sym 'display-no-wait)
    ;; A free camera can legally sit outside the level's vis boxes (under an overhang, high above a
    ;; roof), where the bsp lookup stops updating. Force this level visible while we look at it; it
    ;; is released again on close, so the normal vis path is untouched once the browser is shut.
    (load-state-want-force-vis sym #t))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-set-othercam-sleep ((on? symbol))
  "The TITLE screen's flythrough is an OTHERCAM process ('logo, title-obs.gc:178): its :code loop
   rewrites *camera-other-trans*/*camera-other-matrix* from the logo-cam joint and re-arms
   *camera-look-through-other* EVERY frame, after us — so at the title it always beat the browser's
   camera (measured: 5/5 observed meshes reported the flythrough camera; the orbit never landed).
   SLEEP it while the browser holds the camera — the same process-mask idiom as the player freeze.
   Killing it instead would be wrong twice: title-obs respawns its othercam when the handle dies
   (the fight would restart), and on close the title would have no camera until the respawn.
   Re-applied every browser frame (a title attract cycle can spawn a fresh one); undone on close."
  (set! *global-search-name* (the basic othercam))
  (let ((proc (the process (search-process-tree *active-pool*
                (lambda ((var process)) (= (the type *global-search-name*) (-> var type)))))))
    (when proc
      (if on?
          (logior! (-> proc mask) (process-mask sleep))
          (logclear! (-> proc mask) (process-mask sleep)))))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-freeze-player ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Put the PLAYER PROCESS to sleep so he cannot wander, fall or die while the owner observes. This is
   the engine's own idiom (levels/rolling/rolling-lightning-mole.gc:499) and it does NOT move him:
   execute-process-tree simply skips him (gkernel.gc:1269). Level streaming, the camera and the
   display loop keep running, which is what lets the requested level finish loading."
  (when (and *target* (not (-> obj frozen?)))
    (logior! (-> *target* mask) (process-mask sleep))
    (set! (-> obj frozen?) #t))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-unfreeze-player ((obj mesh-browser))
  (when (and *target* (-> obj frozen?))
    (logclear! (-> *target* mask) (process-mask sleep)))
  (set! (-> obj frozen?) #f)
  (none))

(defmethod mesh-browser-observe-selected mesh-browser ((obj mesh-browser))
  "FREE CAMERA onto the selected mesh. Moves NO player: no continue point, no initialize!, and not a
   single write to (-> *target* root trans). It records the mesh CENTROID as the orbit origin,
   derives the initial camera distance from the BOUNDING BOX, requests the level if it is not
   already active, and enters OBSERVE where mesh-browser-place-camera drives the camera each frame."
  (when (> (-> obj n-filtered) 0)
    (let* ((raw (-> obj view (-> obj sel)))
           (lvl (-> *mesh-browser-levels* (-> obj level-index))))
      (set! (-> obj cur-row) raw)
      ;; ORBIT ORIGIN = this mesh's centroid, straight out of the index (metres -> GOAL units).
      ;; Per-mesh by construction: two meshes with different centroids cannot share a camera spot.
      (set-vector! (-> obj obs-focus)
                   (* (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_CX) 4096.0)
                   (* (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_CY) 4096.0)
                   (* (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_CZ) 4096.0)
                   1.0)
      ;; INITIAL DISTANCE FROM THE BOUNDING BOX diagonal, so a fence post and a cliff face both fill
      ;; the screen.
      (let* ((dx (* (- (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_HIX) (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_LOX)) 4096.0))
             (dy (* (- (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_HIY) (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_LOY)) 4096.0))
             (dz (* (- (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_HIZ) (pc-mesh-index-getf raw MB_GF_LOZ)) 4096.0))
             (diag (sqrtf (+ (* dx dx) (+ (* dy dy) (* dz dz))))))
        (set! (-> obj frame-dist) (fmax 8192.0 (* 0.9 diag))))
      ;; export the identifier so the owner can quote it back without adb.
      (pc-mesh-browser-export! raw)
      ;; the LEVEL may have to come in; the PLAYER stays exactly where he is.
      (mesh-browser-request-level obj (-> lvl sym))
      (set! (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode observe))
      (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none))
      ;; frame it at once, so the first drawn frame is already centred on THIS mesh, and once more
      ;; when the level reports active (need-reframe) in case the request had to stream it in.
      (mesh-browser-frame-mesh obj)
      (set! (-> obj need-reframe) #t)
      (set! (-> obj warp-timer) 0)))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-borrow-world ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Capture and borrow the untouched world — the shared closed->open edge. Extracted VERBATIM from
   mesh-browser-open so the V2 freecam entry (which can open straight from gameplay, no list) borrows
   and restores EXACTLY the same things; mesh-browser-close is the single common give-back."
  ;; Remember the world we are about to borrow. The *target* guard is not decoration: the browser
  ;; is reachable from the TITLE-screen options too, and level-get-target-inside opens with
  ;; (target-pos 0) (engine/level/level.gc:909), which would dereference a #f target.
  (let ((lev (if *target* (level-get-target-inside *level*) (the level #f))))
    (set! (-> obj home-level) (if lev (-> lev name) (the symbol #f))))
  (when *target* (set! (-> obj home-pos quad) (-> *target* root trans quad)))
  ;; snapshot the load-state want list so close can put back the EXACT pair we found, not a guess
  (set! (-> obj saved-want0) (-> *load-state* want 0 name))
  (set! (-> obj saved-want1) (-> *load-state* want 1 name))
  (set! (-> obj saved-disp0) (-> *load-state* want 0 display?))
  (set! (-> obj saved-disp1) (-> *load-state* want 1 display?))
  ;; A free camera wandering across a load boundary would re-issue want-levels under us: the
  ;; boundary test feeds the CAMERA position into the non-player boundaries
  ;; (engine/level/load-boundary.gc:744-758). Suspend boundary crossing while we hold the camera.
  ;; It must be switched off at the SOURCE: (-> *level* border?) is rewritten from
  ;; (-> *setting-control* default border-mode) every single frame (engine/game/settings.gc:232),
  ;; so writing *level* border? directly would survive exactly one frame and prove nothing.
  (set! (-> obj saved-border?) (-> *setting-control* default border-mode))
  (set! (-> *setting-control* default border-mode) #f)
  (mesh-browser-freeze-player obj)
  (none))

(defmethod mesh-browser-open mesh-browser ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Open the browser at the LEVEL picker. Called by the Recharged Settings menu row, and also used as
   the 'back to the level list' action — so anything that must be captured from the untouched world
   is captured ONLY on the closed->open edge."
  (when (= (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode closed))
    (mesh-browser-borrow-world obj))
  (set! (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode levels))
  (set! (-> obj level-index) 0)
  (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none))
  (set! (-> obj scroll-f) 0.0)
  (set! (-> obj scroll-vel) 0.0)
  ;; the picker scrolls with the SAME physics as the mesh list (25 levels do not fit one page)
  (set! (-> obj n-filtered) (length *mesh-browser-levels*))
  (set! (-> obj sel) 0)
  ;; Tell the Android overlay we own the screen: it suspends the virtual gamepad and starts
  ;; forwarding RAW multi-touch. Without this the browser receives no touch events at all.
  (pc-mb-set-active! 1)
  (mesh-browser-sync-touch)
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-open! ()
  "Plain-function opener the Recharged Settings button calls (forward-declared in progress-pc.gc)."
  (mesh-browser-open *mesh-browser*)
  (none))

;; defined near the end of this file, but called from mesh-browser-close below: the close path
;; writes one final mode=CLOSED dump so the state file records the close itself.
(define-extern mesh-browser-dump-state (function mesh-browser none))

(defmethod mesh-browser-close mesh-browser ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Close the browser and hand the world back exactly as we found it: camera to the player, forced
   visibility released, the player's own level re-wanted, load boundaries re-armed, player awake."
  (set! (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode closed))
  (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none))
  (set! (-> obj reload-timer) 0)
  ;; release the camera: the stock follow-camera resumes on the very next frame (nothing to unwind,
  ;; *camera-look-through-other* decays to 0 by itself once we stop re-arming it).
  (set! *camera-look-through-other* 0)
  (when (-> obj browse-level) (load-state-want-force-vis (-> obj browse-level) #f))
  ;; put back the EXACT want pair we found at open (not "the player's level and nothing else" —
  ;; that would silently drop the neighbouring level when the browser was opened near a boundary)
  (load-state-want-levels (-> obj saved-want0) (-> obj saved-want1))
  (when (-> obj saved-want0) (load-state-want-display-level (-> obj saved-want0) (-> obj saved-disp0)))
  (when (-> obj saved-want1) (load-state-want-display-level (-> obj saved-want1) (-> obj saved-disp1)))
  (set! (-> *setting-control* default border-mode) (-> obj saved-border?))
  (mesh-browser-set-othercam-sleep #f)
  (mesh-browser-unfreeze-player obj)
  (set! (-> obj browse-level) (the symbol #f))
  ;; drop any freecam render target: the renderer must never keep hiding/checkering a mesh after
  ;; the browser is gone (pc-mb-target-clear! also clears the C++ hide/checker/gizmo flags).
  (pc-mb-target-clear!)
  (set! (-> obj fc-target) -1)
  ;; V2.3: disarm the reticle hover ray — the render thread must stop highlighting once the
  ;; freecam is gone (the per-frame arm lives in mesh-browser-input-freecam only).
  (let ((dis (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
    (set-vector! dis 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.0)
    (pc-mb-hover-ray! (-> obj fc-pos) dis 0))
  ;; hand touch back to the virtual gamepad — the overlay is byte-identical from here on.
  (pc-mb-set-active! 0)
  ;; one FINAL state dump so the file says mode=CLOSED. The state file is the evidence channel: a
  ;; harness (or the supervisor reading it back for the owner) that samples it after an EXIT tap
  ;; must see the close happen, not the last OBSERVE state frozen in place.
  (mesh-browser-dump-state obj)
  (none))

;; ---- LEVEL PICKER ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defun mesh-browser-draw-levels ((obj mesh-browser) (buf dma-buffer))
  (mesh-browser-rect buf 0.0 0.0 1.0 1.0 (new 'static 'rgba :r #x08 :g #x08 :b #x14 :a #xd0))
  (mesh-browser-text buf "MESH BROWSER - PICK A LEVEL" 0.02 0.055 (font-color yellow))
  (mb-button buf 0.80 MB_BTN_TOP 0.99 MB_BTN_BOT "CLOSE" #f)
  ;; 25 levels do not fit one page, so the picker pages/scrolls exactly like the mesh list.
  (let ((n (length *mesh-browser-levels*))
        (rh (mb-row-h))
        (top (the int (-> obj scroll-f))))
    (dotimes (i MB_PAGE)
      (let ((r (+ top i)))
        (when (and (>= r 0) (< r n))
          (let* ((y0 (+ MB_LIST_TOP (* (the float i) rh)))
                 (lvl (-> *mesh-browser-levels* r))
                 (sel? (= r (-> obj level-index))))
            (when sel?
              (mesh-browser-rect buf 0.01 y0 MB_TRACK_X0 (+ y0 rh)
                                 (new 'static 'rgba :r #x30 :g #x60 :b #xa0 :a #xa0)))
            (mesh-browser-text buf (-> lvl index-name) 0.04 (+ y0 (* 0.72 rh))
                               (if sel? (font-color white) (font-color cyan))))))))
  (mesh-browser-draw-scrollbar obj buf)
  (mesh-browser-text buf "TAP A LEVEL  -  SWIPE TO SCROLL  /  D-PAD + X" 0.02 (+ MB_FOOT_TOP 0.055)
                     (font-color green))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-input-levels ((obj mesh-browser))
  (let ((n (length *mesh-browser-levels*))
        (rh (mb-row-h)))
    ;; the picker borrows the mesh list's row count so the shared scroll physics apply to it too
    (set! (-> obj n-filtered) n)
    (cond
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 up)
       (set! (-> obj level-index) (mod (+ (-> obj level-index) (+ n -1)) n))
       (set! (-> obj sel) (-> obj level-index))
       (mesh-browser-list-keep-sel-visible obj))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 down)
       (set! (-> obj level-index) (mod (+ (-> obj level-index) 1) n))
       (set! (-> obj sel) (-> obj level-index))
       (mesh-browser-list-keep-sel-visible obj))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 x) (mesh-browser-enter-list obj))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 triangle) (mesh-browser-close obj))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 circle) (mesh-browser-close obj)))
    ;; TOUCH: swipe/fling/handle to scroll, then tap the level row itself — one tap, no cursor.
    (mesh-browser-list-scroll-physics obj)
    (when (-> *mb-gest* tap?)
      (cond
        ((mb-tap-in? 0.80 MB_BTN_TOP 0.99 MB_BTN_BOT) (mesh-browser-close obj))
        ((mb-tap-in? MB_TRACK_X0 MB_LIST_TOP 1.0 MB_LIST_BOT)
         (let* ((span (- MB_LIST_BOT MB_LIST_TOP))
                (t0 (fmin 1.0 (fmax 0.0 (/ (- (-> *mb-gest* tap-y) MB_LIST_TOP) span)))))
           (set! (-> obj scroll-f) (* t0 (mesh-browser-scroll-max obj)))
           (mesh-browser-clamp-scroll obj)))
        (else
         (let ((top (the int (-> obj scroll-f))))
           (dotimes (i MB_PAGE)
             (let ((r (+ top i))
                   (y0 (+ MB_LIST_TOP (* (the float i) rh))))
               (when (and (< r n) (mb-tap-in? 0.01 y0 MB_TRACK_X0 (+ y0 rh)))
                 (set! (-> obj level-index) r)
                 (mesh-browser-enter-list obj)))))))))
  (none))

;; ---- MESH LIST ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; village1 alone holds 3613 rows. Stepping that one row at a time is unusable by construction, so
;; the list is driven the way every phone list is: swipe to scroll with inertia, plus a right-edge
;; fast-scroll handle that crosses the whole 3613-row range in a single drag.

(defun mesh-browser-draw-list ((obj mesh-browser) (buf dma-buffer))
  (mesh-browser-rect buf 0.0 0.0 1.0 1.0 (new 'static 'rgba :r #x08 :g #x08 :b #x14 :a #xc0))
  ;; header: BACK + the four filters, as finger-sized buttons
  (mb-button buf 0.005 MB_BTN_TOP 0.185 MB_BTN_BOT "BACK" #f)
  (mb-button buf 0.195 MB_BTN_TOP 0.385 MB_BTN_BOT "ALL"
             (= (-> obj filter) (mesh-browser-filter all)))
  (mb-button buf 0.395 MB_BTN_TOP 0.585 MB_BTN_BOT "FAILING"
             (= (-> obj filter) (mesh-browser-filter failing)))
  (mb-button buf 0.595 MB_BTN_TOP 0.785 MB_BTN_BOT "TFRAG"
             (= (-> obj filter) (mesh-browser-filter tfrag)))
  (mb-button buf 0.795 MB_BTN_TOP 0.985 MB_BTN_BOT "TIE"
             (= (-> obj filter) (mesh-browser-filter tie)))
  (mesh-browser-text buf
    (string-format "~S  ~D/~D MESHES  WORST FIRST" (-> obj level-buf) (-> obj n-filtered) (-> obj n-total))
    0.02 0.165 (font-color yellow))
  ;; rows
  (let ((rh (mb-row-h))
        (top (the int (-> obj scroll-f))))
    (dotimes (i MB_PAGE)
      (let ((r (+ top i)))
        (when (and (>= r 0) (< r (-> obj n-filtered)))
          (let* ((raw (-> obj view r))
                 (y0 (+ MB_LIST_TOP (* (the float i) rh)))
                 (sel? (= r (-> obj sel)))
                 (sys (if (= (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_SYSTEM) 1) "TIE  " "TFRAG"))
                 (graded (= (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_GRADED) 1))
                 (asign (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_ASIGN))
                 ;; colour = grade severity: red < 50%, orange < 100%, green 100%, cyan ungraded
                 (col (cond ((not graded) (font-color cyan))
                            ((< asign 5000) (font-color red))
                            ((< asign 10000) (font-color orange))
                            (else (font-color green)))))
            (pc-mesh-index-name! raw (-> obj name-buf))
            (when sel?
              (mesh-browser-rect buf 0.005 y0 MB_TRACK_X0 (+ y0 rh)
                                 (new 'static 'rgba :r #x30 :g #x60 :b #xa0 :a #xa0)))
            (mesh-browser-text buf
              (string-format "~4D ~S ~S  ~S" raw sys (-> obj name-buf) (mb-grade-string obj raw))
              0.02 (+ y0 (* 0.74 rh)) (if sel? (font-color white) col)))))))
  ;; fast-scroll handle: the ONLY practical way across thousands of rows in one gesture.
  (mesh-browser-draw-scrollbar obj buf)
  ;; footer
  (mb-button buf 0.005 MB_FOOT_TOP 0.235 MB_FOOT_BOT "OPEN" #f)
  (mesh-browser-text buf
    (string-format "ROW ~D  -  SWIPE TO SCROLL, DRAG THE BAR, TAP A ROW" (-> obj sel))
    0.26 (+ MB_FOOT_TOP 0.058) (font-color green))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-input-list ((obj mesh-browser))
  ;; gamepad
  (let ((moved? #f))
    (cond
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 up) (set! (-> obj sel) (max 0 (+ (-> obj sel) -1))) (set! moved? #t))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 down)
       (set! (-> obj sel) (min (max 0 (+ (-> obj n-filtered) -1)) (+ (-> obj sel) 1)))
       (set! moved? #t))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 left) (set! (-> obj sel) (max 0 (+ (-> obj sel) (- MB_PAGE)))) (set! moved? #t))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 right)
       (set! (-> obj sel) (min (max 0 (+ (-> obj n-filtered) -1)) (+ (-> obj sel) MB_PAGE)))
       (set! moved? #t))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 l1)
       (mesh-browser-cycle-filter obj (the-as mesh-browser-filter (mod (+ (the int (-> obj filter)) 3) 4))))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 r1)
       (mesh-browser-cycle-filter obj (the-as mesh-browser-filter (mod (+ (the int (-> obj filter)) 1) 4))))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 x) (mesh-browser-observe-selected obj))
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 triangle) (mesh-browser-open obj))   ;; back to level picker
      ((cpad-pressed? 0 circle) (mesh-browser-open obj)))
    (when moved? (mesh-browser-list-keep-sel-visible obj)))
  ;; TOUCH — scrolling first, then the discrete taps
  (mesh-browser-list-scroll-physics obj)
  (when (-> *mb-gest* tap?)
    (cond
      ((mb-tap-in? 0.005 MB_BTN_TOP 0.185 MB_BTN_BOT) (mesh-browser-open obj))
      ((mb-tap-in? 0.195 MB_BTN_TOP 0.385 MB_BTN_BOT)
       (mesh-browser-cycle-filter obj (mesh-browser-filter all)))
      ((mb-tap-in? 0.395 MB_BTN_TOP 0.585 MB_BTN_BOT)
       (mesh-browser-cycle-filter obj (mesh-browser-filter failing)))
      ((mb-tap-in? 0.595 MB_BTN_TOP 0.785 MB_BTN_BOT)
       (mesh-browser-cycle-filter obj (mesh-browser-filter tfrag)))
      ((mb-tap-in? 0.795 MB_BTN_TOP 0.985 MB_BTN_BOT)
       (mesh-browser-cycle-filter obj (mesh-browser-filter tie)))
      ((mb-tap-in? 0.005 MB_FOOT_TOP 0.235 MB_FOOT_BOT) (mesh-browser-observe-selected obj))
      ;; a tap on the fast-scroll track jumps straight to that position
      ((mb-tap-in? MB_TRACK_X0 MB_LIST_TOP 1.0 MB_LIST_BOT)
       (let* ((span (- MB_LIST_BOT MB_LIST_TOP))
              (t0 (fmin 1.0 (fmax 0.0 (/ (- (-> *mb-gest* tap-y) MB_LIST_TOP) span)))))
         (set! (-> obj scroll-f) (* t0 (mesh-browser-scroll-max obj)))
         (mesh-browser-clamp-scroll obj)))
      (else
       ;; a row: tap it to select, tap the selected row again to open it
       (let ((rh (mb-row-h))
             (top (the int (-> obj scroll-f))))
         (dotimes (i MB_PAGE)
           (let ((r (+ top i))
                 (y0 (+ MB_LIST_TOP (* (the float i) (mb-row-h)))))
             (when (and (< r (-> obj n-filtered))
                        (mb-tap-in? 0.0 y0 MB_TRACK_X0 (+ y0 rh)))
               (if (= r (-> obj sel))
                   (mesh-browser-observe-selected obj)
                   (set! (-> obj sel) r)))))))))
  (none))

;; ---- OBSERVE --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; After the warp settles the browser takes the camera outright (*camera-look-through-other*, the
;; cutscene hook: "camera HERE, looking THERE") instead of borrowing cam-orbit. cam-orbit reads the
;; right stick directly out of *cpad-list* and stores a single azimuth with no elevation term, so
;; driving it from gestures would mean fighting it for the stick every frame. Owning the camera makes
;; orbit / elevation / zoom exactly three numbers this file controls, which is what lets a finger
;; drive them.

(define *mb-tod-hour* 12.0)          ;; the hour the owner is holding
(define *mb-tod-hold?* #f)

;; observe button grid: 2 rows x 7 finger-sized cells
(defconstant MB_RA_TOP 0.720)
(defconstant MB_RA_BOT 0.845)
(defconstant MB_RB_TOP 0.855)
(defconstant MB_RB_BOT 0.980)

;; ELEVATION RANGE — owner: "elevation du dessous au dessus (y compris a la verticale, pour voir la
;; face inferieure d'un surplomb)". 1.5533 rad = 89 degrees: very nearly straight down onto a roof,
;; and very nearly straight up at the underside of an overhang. It stops one degree short of the
;; pole on purpose — at exactly 90 the forward vector is parallel to "down" and
;; forward-down->inv-matrix (engine/geometry/geometry.gc:255) has no basis left to build.
(defconstant MB_EL_MIN -1.5533)
(defconstant MB_EL_MAX 1.5533)

(defun mb-cell-x0 ((i int)) (+ (* (the float i) 0.14285) 0.003))
(defun mb-cell-x1 ((i int)) (- (* (the float (+ i 1)) 0.14285) 0.003))

;; NOTE: there used to be a mesh-browser-pin-jak here, writing (-> *target* root trans) every frame.
;; It is GONE, deliberately: the owner's correction is that selecting a mesh must not move the
;; player at all. Nothing in this file writes a player position any more — the only way to hold him
;; still is mesh-browser-freeze-player, which sleeps his process where he stands.

(defun mesh-browser-place-camera ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Put the camera on the orbit sphere around the mesh centroid and aim it at the centroid.
   The MESH SPIN is folded in here: it advances the camera azimuth, and mesh-browser-apply-light-spin
   advances the sun azimuth by the SAME angle. Moving the camera and the light together about the
   centroid is a rigid rotation of the object relative to both — i.e. exactly what spinning the mesh
   under a fixed light looks like on the mesh itself. (Only the surrounding world does not spin with
   it; the geometry is baked in place and cannot actually be rotated without a per-mesh model matrix
   in the renderer, which would be a render-path change and this phase only observes.)"
  (let ((pos (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (fwd (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (dwn (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
    (let* ((az (mb-pi-wrap (+ (-> obj obs-az) (-> obj spin))))
           (el (-> obj obs-el))
           (d (-> obj obs-dist))
           (hr (* d (cos-rad el))))
      (set-vector! pos
                   (+ (-> obj obs-focus x) (* hr (sin-rad az)))
                   (+ (-> obj obs-focus y) (* d (sin-rad el)))
                   (+ (-> obj obs-focus z) (* hr (cos-rad az)))
                   1.0))
    (vector-! fwd (-> obj obs-focus) pos)
    (vector-normalize! fwd 1.0)
    (set-vector! dwn 0.0 -1.0 0.0 0.0)
    (forward-down->inv-matrix *camera-other-matrix* fwd dwn)
    (set! (-> *camera-other-trans* quad) (-> pos quad))
    ;; re-armed every frame; it decays to 0 on its own once we stop, so the stock camera resumes
    ;; with no state to unwind.
    (set! *camera-look-through-other* 2))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-apply-light-spin ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Rotate both sky suns about world Y by the mesh-spin angle, so the light turns WITH the camera and
   the object appears to spin under a fixed light. No-op at spin 0, so lighting is untouched until
   the owner spins the mesh."
  (#when FLAG_PBR
    (when (!= (-> obj spin) 0.0)
      ;; UNITS: vector-rotate-around-y! (engine/math/vector.gc:723) calls (cos)/(sin), which are the
      ;; ROTATION-UNIT versions — 65536 units to a full turn (trigonometry.gc:162, and it does
      ;; (the int arg0) first, so any angle below 1.0 rad truncated to ZERO). Passing radians made
      ;; the light spin a silent no-op, i.e. spinning the mesh only moved the camera. 10430.378 =
      ;; 65536 / 2pi converts.
      (let ((v (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
            (rot (* (-> obj spin) 10430.378)))
        (vector-rotate-around-y! v (-> *sky-parms* upload-data sun 0 pos) rot)
        (pc-set-pbr-sky-sun! v)
        (vector-rotate-around-y! v (-> *sky-parms* upload-data sun 1 pos) rot)
        (pc-set-pbr-green-sun! v))))
  (none))

(defun mb-disp-name ()
  (case (-> *pc-settings* pbr-displacement)
    ((0) "OFF")
    ((1) "PARALLAX")
    ((2) "TESSELLATION")
    (else "?")))

(defun mesh-browser-bump-disp ((obj mesh-browser) (dir int))
  ;; drive the pc-settings field the menu owns; update-to-os re-asserts it to C++.
  ;; WRAPS (0 1 2 0 ...) like every other carousel: with a clamp, a single DISP+ tap while the
  ;; device already sits at TESSELLATION is a silent no-op — the finger does something only
  ;; sometimes, which reads as "touch is broken" precisely when the owner has been testing tess.
  (set! (-> *pc-settings* pbr-displacement) (mod (+ (-> *pc-settings* pbr-displacement) dir 3) 3))
  ;; V2.1: ALSO push DIRECTLY, event-driven. Measured on the Redmi at the title freecam: the
  ;; update-to-os per-frame push chain lagged ~6-7 s behind the variable (the renderer-side
  ;; rtf_relief counter exposed it), so a button press looked dead for seconds — the owner's
  ;; "activer/desactiver le relief fonctionne pas" in one measurement. Direct push = same-frame
  ;; effect, same pattern as pc-mb-hide-set! (which is instant); update-to-os keeps re-asserting
  ;; the same value afterwards, so there is no fight.
  (#when FLAG_PBR
    (pc-set-pbr-displacement! (the int (-> *pc-settings* pbr-displacement))))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-bump-relief ((obj mesh-browser) (d float))
  (set! (-> *pc-settings* pbr-texture-relief)
        (fmax 0.0 (fmin 3.0 (+ (-> *pc-settings* pbr-texture-relief) d))))
  ;; [mb-diag] names WHEN the bump executed (GK_STDOUT), paired with the C++ [mb-diag] push line.
  (format 0 "[mb-diag-goal] bump-relief -> ~f~%" (-> *pc-settings* pbr-texture-relief))
  ;; V2.1 direct push — see mesh-browser-bump-disp for the measured 6-7 s update-to-os lag.
  (#when FLAG_PBR
    (pc-set-pbr-texture-relief! (the int (* 100.0 (-> *pc-settings* pbr-texture-relief)))))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-set-tod ((obj mesh-browser) (h float))
  (set! *mb-tod-hold?* #t)
  (set! *mb-tod-hour* (mb-wrap h 24.0))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-bump-tod ((obj mesh-browser) (d float))
  (mesh-browser-set-tod obj (+ *mb-tod-hour* d))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-bump-spin ((obj mesh-browser) (d float))
  (set! (-> obj spin) (mb-wrap (+ (-> obj spin) d) 6.2832))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-toggle-checker ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Flip the real-texture <-> checker global. The pattern is substituted when a texture is UPLOADED
   (game/graphics/opengl_renderer/loader/LoaderStages.cpp:149), so the browsed level has to come
   round again for the flip to show. It used to do that by re-warping the player; now it re-requests
   the LEVEL instead — same effect on the textures, and the player never moves."
  (set! (-> obj checker?) (not (-> obj checker?)))
  (pc-set-mesh-browser-checker! (if (-> obj checker?) 1 0))
  (set! (-> obj reload-timer) 1)
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-tick-reload ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Drop the browsed level from the want list for a few frames, then ask for it again, so its textures
   are uploaded afresh with the new checker mode. Driven from the per-frame OBSERVE update. The
   player's own level stays wanted throughout, so the ground under him is never discarded."
  (when (> (-> obj reload-timer) 0)
    (+! (-> obj reload-timer) 1)
    (cond
      ((= (-> obj reload-timer) 2)
       (if (-> obj home-level)
           (load-state-want-levels (-> obj home-level) (the symbol #f))
           (load-state-want-levels (the symbol #f) (the symbol #f))))
      ((>= (-> obj reload-timer) 16)
       (mesh-browser-request-level obj (-> obj browse-level))
       (set! (-> obj need-reframe) #t)
       (set! (-> obj warp-timer) 0)
       (set! (-> obj reload-timer) 0))))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-exit-observe ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Leave OBSERVE back to the mesh list, restoring the normal camera. If a checker reload was still
   mid-flight the level has been dropped from the want list and not yet re-asked for — finish that
   here, or the level would simply stay unloaded and the counter would resume mid-sequence."
  (set! *camera-look-through-other* 0)
  ;; give the camera channel back to whoever owned it (title flythrough othercam, cutscene cam)
  (mesh-browser-set-othercam-sleep #f)
  (when (> (-> obj reload-timer) 0)
    (set! (-> obj reload-timer) 0)
    (mesh-browser-request-level obj (-> obj browse-level)))
  (set! (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode list))
  (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-draw-observe ((obj mesh-browser) (buf dma-buffer))
  (let ((raw (-> obj cur-row)))
    (pc-mesh-index-name! raw (-> obj name-buf))
    (mesh-browser-rect buf 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.30 (new 'static 'rgba :r #x08 :g #x08 :b #x14 :a #x90))
    ;; the identifier the owner quotes back to us (also exported to files/mesh_select.txt).
    (mesh-browser-text buf
      (string-format "MESH ~S / ~S  ~S  SHELL ~D  TEX ~D"
                     (-> obj level-buf) (-> obj name-buf)
                     (if (= (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_SYSTEM) 1) "TIE" "TFRAG")
                     (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_SHELL) (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_TEX))
      0.02 0.055 (font-color white))
    ;; THE cross-check: show the offline grade so the owner can confirm OR refute it.
    (mesh-browser-text buf
      (string-format "OFFLINE GRADE A_SIGN=~S  (file mesh_select.txt)" (mb-grade-string obj raw))
      0.02 0.105 (font-color yellow))
    (if *mb-tod-hold?*
        (format (clear (-> obj sub-buf)) "~fH" *mb-tod-hour*)
        (format (clear (-> obj sub-buf)) "CYCLE"))
    (mesh-browser-text buf
      (string-format "TEXTURE=~S  DISPLACEMENT=~S  RELIEF=~f  TOD=~S"
                     (if (-> obj checker?) "CHECKER" "REAL")
                     (mb-disp-name)
                     (-> *pc-settings* pbr-texture-relief)
                     (-> obj sub-buf))
      0.02 0.155 (font-color cyan))
    (mesh-browser-text buf
      (string-format "SPIN=~f RAD   DRAG=ORBIT  PINCH=ZOOM  2-FINGER DRAG=SPIN MESH" (-> obj spin))
      0.02 0.205 (font-color green))
    ;; every control reachable by finger — no gamepad, no adb
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 0) MB_RA_TOP (mb-cell-x1 0) MB_RA_BOT
               (if (-> obj checker?) "REAL" "CHECKER") (-> obj checker?))
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 1) MB_RA_TOP (mb-cell-x1 1) MB_RA_BOT "DISP-" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 2) MB_RA_TOP (mb-cell-x1 2) MB_RA_BOT "DISP+" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 3) MB_RA_TOP (mb-cell-x1 3) MB_RA_BOT "REL-" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 4) MB_RA_TOP (mb-cell-x1 4) MB_RA_BOT "REL+" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 5) MB_RA_TOP (mb-cell-x1 5) MB_RA_BOT "SPIN-" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 6) MB_RA_TOP (mb-cell-x1 6) MB_RA_BOT "SPIN+" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 0) MB_RB_TOP (mb-cell-x1 0) MB_RB_BOT "TOD-" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 1) MB_RB_TOP (mb-cell-x1 1) MB_RB_BOT "TOD+" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 2) MB_RB_TOP (mb-cell-x1 2) MB_RB_BOT "DAY" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 3) MB_RB_TOP (mb-cell-x1 3) MB_RB_BOT "NIGHT" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 4) MB_RB_TOP (mb-cell-x1 4) MB_RB_BOT "RESET" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 5) MB_RB_TOP (mb-cell-x1 5) MB_RB_BOT "LIST" #f)
    (mb-button buf (mb-cell-x0 6) MB_RB_TOP (mb-cell-x1 6) MB_RB_BOT "EXIT" #f))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-handle-obs-tap ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Tap on the button grid = the matching action. Every rect tested here is the same rect
   mesh-browser-draw-observe drew, via mb-cell-x0/x1 — they cannot drift apart."
  (when (-> *mb-gest* tap?)
    (dotimes (i 7)
      (when (mb-tap-in? (mb-cell-x0 i) MB_RA_TOP (mb-cell-x1 i) MB_RA_BOT)
        (case i
          ((0) (mesh-browser-toggle-checker obj))
          ((1) (mesh-browser-bump-disp obj -1))
          ((2) (mesh-browser-bump-disp obj 1))
          ((3) (mesh-browser-bump-relief obj -0.25))
          ((4) (mesh-browser-bump-relief obj 0.25))
          ((5) (mesh-browser-bump-spin obj -0.196))
          ((6) (mesh-browser-bump-spin obj 0.196))))
      (when (mb-tap-in? (mb-cell-x0 i) MB_RB_TOP (mb-cell-x1 i) MB_RB_BOT)
        (case i
          ((0) (mesh-browser-bump-tod obj -1.0))
          ((1) (mesh-browser-bump-tod obj 1.0))
          ((2) (mesh-browser-set-tod obj 12.0))
          ((3) (mesh-browser-set-tod obj 0.0))
          ((4) (mesh-browser-frame-mesh obj))
          ((5) (mesh-browser-exit-observe obj))
          ((6) (mesh-browser-close obj))))))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-observe-gestures ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Drag = orbit (horizontal azimuth, vertical elevation — two distinct drag axes).
   Pinch = zoom. Two-finger drag = spin the mesh. All in the view area, i.e. anywhere above the
   button grid."
  (let ((g *mb-gest*))
    (when (-> g down?)
      (set! (-> obj drag)
            (if (mb-down-in? 0.0 0.0 1.0 (- MB_RA_TOP 0.005))
                (mesh-browser-drag orbit)
                (mesh-browser-drag none))))
    (cond
      ;; TWO FINGERS: always zoom/spin, wherever the gesture began. No button uses two fingers, so a
      ;; pinch is unambiguous — gating it on where the FIRST finger happened to land would drop the
      ;; gesture whenever that finger started on the button grid.
      ((>= (-> g fingers) 2)
       ;; pinch: separation grows -> pull the camera in
       (when (!= (-> g pinch) 0.0)
         (set! (-> obj obs-dist)
               (fmax 2048.0 (fmin 819200.0 (* (-> obj obs-dist) (- 1.0 (* 2.2 (-> g pinch))))))))
       ;; two-finger horizontal travel spins the mesh (camera + light together)
       (when (!= (-> g d2x) 0.0)
         (mesh-browser-bump-spin obj (* -3.2 (-> g d2x)))))
      ;; ONE FINGER: orbit, but only if the drag STARTED in the view area, so a finger sliding off a
      ;; button never yanks the camera.
      ((and (= (-> g fingers) 1) (= (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag orbit)))
       (set! (-> obj obs-az) (mb-wrap (+ (-> obj obs-az) (* -3.2 (-> g dx))) 6.2832))
       ;; elevation is clamped short of the poles: forward-down->inv-matrix needs a forward vector
       ;; that is not parallel to "down".
       (set! (-> obj obs-el) (fmax MB_EL_MIN (fmin MB_EL_MAX (+ (-> obj obs-el) (* 2.4 (-> g dy))))))))
    (when (-> g up?) (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none))))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-input-observe ((obj mesh-browser))
  ;; The camera is already on this mesh from frame one (mesh-browser-observe-selected framed it).
  ;; If the level had to stream in, frame it once more when it reports 'active, so the framing is
  ;; right even when the geometry arrived late. Never waits on *target* — the player is irrelevant
  ;; to this camera.
  (+! (-> obj warp-timer) 1)
  (mesh-browser-tick-reload obj)
  (when (and (-> obj need-reframe)
             (> (-> obj warp-timer) 8)
             (or (= (level-status *level* (-> obj browse-level)) 'active)
                 (> (-> obj warp-timer) 900)))
    (mesh-browser-frame-mesh obj)
    (set! (-> obj need-reframe) #f))
  ;; gamepad: the browser owns the camera now, so it reads the sticks itself.
  (let ((rx (- (the float (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 rightx)) 128.0))
        (ry (- (the float (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 righty)) 128.0))
        (ly (- (the float (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 lefty)) 128.0)))
    (when (> (fabs rx) 24.0) (set! (-> obj obs-az) (mb-wrap (+ (-> obj obs-az) (* rx 0.0005)) 6.2832)))
    (when (> (fabs ry) 24.0)
      (set! (-> obj obs-el) (fmax MB_EL_MIN (fmin MB_EL_MAX (+ (-> obj obs-el) (* ry -0.0004))))))
    (when (> (fabs ly) 24.0)
      (set! (-> obj obs-dist) (fmax 2048.0 (fmin 819200.0 (* (-> obj obs-dist) (+ 1.0 (* ly 0.00015))))))))
  (cond
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 square) (mesh-browser-toggle-checker obj))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 l2) (mesh-browser-bump-disp obj -1))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 r2) (mesh-browser-bump-disp obj 1))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 up) (mesh-browser-bump-relief obj 0.25))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 down) (mesh-browser-bump-relief obj -0.25))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 left) (mesh-browser-bump-tod obj -1.0))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 right) (mesh-browser-bump-tod obj 1.0))
    ((cpad-hold? 0 l1) (mesh-browser-bump-spin obj -0.03))
    ((cpad-hold? 0 r1) (mesh-browser-bump-spin obj 0.03))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 triangle) (mesh-browser-exit-observe obj))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 circle) (mesh-browser-exit-observe obj)))
  ;; touch
  (mesh-browser-observe-gestures obj)
  (mesh-browser-handle-obs-tap obj)
  ;; hold the view on the mesh. NOTE what is NOT here any more: nothing touches the player.
  (when (= (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode observe))
    ;; every frame, not just on entry: a title attract cycle can spawn a FRESH othercam mid-observe
    (mesh-browser-set-othercam-sleep #t)
    (mesh-browser-place-camera obj)
    (mesh-browser-apply-light-spin obj)
    ;; hold the chosen hour (re-asserted every frame, or the day/night cycle ticks it forward)
    (when (and *mb-tod-hold?* *time-of-day-proc*)
      (set-time-of-day *mb-tod-hour*)))
  (none))

;; ---- V2 FREECAM ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Owner, 2026-07-30: the list UI "est a chier" — what he wants is to FLY, reticle-first: enter a
;; freecam fully detached from Jak (R3 or the overlay button), fly with the left stick in ALL
;; directions including the air, look with the right stick / touch area, put the crosshair on a mesh
;; and R1/R2 to target it (its NAME in plain text), L1/L2 hide/show it, Square checker-tess it,
;; Circle its NORMAL GIZMOS (the dream tool for the orientation hunt — he can now SEE an inward
;; normal), Triangle to defocus. The list survives as secondary UI; going back to it is via the menu.

(defun mesh-browser-freecam-fwd ((obj mesh-browser) (out vector))
  "The freecam look direction from yaw/pitch: (sin yaw * cos pitch, sin pitch, cos yaw * cos pitch).
   Shared by the reticle pick ray, the fly step and the per-frame camera matrix so all three agree
   by construction. mb-pi-wrap before EVERY sin-rad/cos-rad — yaw lives in [0,2pi) and those
   polynomials diverge outside [-pi,pi] (see the trap doc at mb-pi-wrap)."
  (let* ((yw (mb-pi-wrap (-> obj fc-yaw)))
         (pt (mb-pi-wrap (-> obj fc-pitch)))
         (cp (cos-rad pt)))
    (set-vector! out (* (sin-rad yw) cp) (sin-rad pt) (* (cos-rad yw) cp) 0.0))
  out)

(defun mesh-browser-freecam-refresh-levels ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Tell the C++ picker which (up to 2) ACTIVE levels to slab-test against. Reads the same level
   slots the engine streams into (level0/level1 — level-default is never a wantable level), and the
   same 'active status test V1's reframe uses via level-status (which just returns (-> lev status),
   engine/level/level.gc:262). An unused slot is the empty string."
  (let ((slot 0))
    (dotimes (i 2)
      (let ((lev (-> *level* level i)))
        (when (and (= (-> lev status) 'active) (< slot 2))
          ;; the level symbol's print name IS the index-name for all 25 shipped levels
          (format (clear (if (zero? slot) (-> obj fc-lvl0) (-> obj fc-lvl1))) "~A" (-> lev name))
          (+! slot 1))))
    (when (zero? slot) (format (clear (-> obj fc-lvl0)) ""))
    (when (< slot 2) (format (clear (-> obj fc-lvl1)) "")))
  (pc-mb-pick-levels! (-> obj fc-lvl0) (-> obj fc-lvl1))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-freecam-pick ((obj mesh-browser) (dir int))
  "V2.1 reticle pick, phase 1 (REQUEST): ray from the freecam through the screen centre, slab-tested
   against every mesh AABB of the active levels — AND armed for the render thread's TRIANGLE
   ray-test (v2.1: AABB order alone ranked camera-enclosing junk first; a single R1 then targeted a
   mesh the owner could not see, which is why every toggle read as dead). The pick COMPLETES in
   mesh-browser-freecam-pick-poll a frame or two later, once the renderers have measured the real
   surface distances. dir +1 (R1) / -1 (R2) still CYCLES through overlapping candidates."
  (when (zero? (-> obj fc-pick-wait))  ;; a pick is a click, not a queue — ignore while pending
    (mesh-browser-freecam-refresh-levels obj)
    (let ((org (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
          (dirv (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
      (set! (-> org quad) (-> obj fc-pos quad))
      (mesh-browser-freecam-fwd obj dirv)
      (set! (-> obj fc-pick-n) (pc-mb-pick! org dirv)))
    (set! (-> obj fc-pick-dir) dir)
    (set! (-> obj fc-pick-wait) 1))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-freecam-pick-poll ((obj mesh-browser))
  "V2.1 reticle pick, phase 2 (COMPLETE): once the render thread's triangle results are in
   (pc-mb-pick-ready? re-sorts the candidates by REAL surface distance), select and target. The
   40-frame timeout completes with the AABB order — a level whose renderer never ran has nothing
   on screen to pick anyway."
  (when (> (-> obj fc-pick-wait) 0)
    (+! (-> obj fc-pick-wait) 1)
    (let ((rdy (pc-mb-pick-ready?)))
     (when (or (> rdy 0) (> (-> obj fc-pick-wait) 40))
      ;; [mb-diag] completion trace: waited N frames; 41+ = TIMEOUT fallback (AABB order).
      (format 0 "[mb-diag-goal] pick complete wait=~D rdy=~D~%" (-> obj fc-pick-wait) rdy)
      (set! (-> obj fc-pick-wait) 0)
      ;; V2.2: ready returns 1 + the FOLDED candidate count — the C++ side DROPS box-only
      ;; candidates once real triangle hits exist (an AABB on the ray whose actual surface is
      ;; not = the "picks meshes behind others / out of view" class). Refresh n to match, or the
      ;; cycle below would index freed entries.
      (when (> rdy 0)
        (set! (-> obj fc-pick-n) (+ rdy -1)))
      (let ((n (-> obj fc-pick-n))
            (dir (-> obj fc-pick-dir)))
        (when (> n 0)
          ;; where does the CURRENT target sit in the candidate list?
          (let ((p -1))
            (dotimes (i n)
              (when (and (= (pc-mb-pick-geti i MB_PK_ROW) (-> obj fc-target))
                         (= (pc-mb-pick-geti i MB_PK_SLOT) (-> obj fc-target-slot)))
                (set! p i)))
            (let* ((idx (if (>= p 0)
                            (mod (+ p dir n) n)           ;; cycle from the current target
                            (if (>= dir 0) 0 (+ n -1))))  ;; fresh pick: R1 = nearest SEEN surface
                   (row (pc-mb-pick-geti idx MB_PK_ROW))
                   (slot (pc-mb-pick-geti idx MB_PK_SLOT)))
              (pc-mb-target-set! row slot)
              (set! (-> obj fc-target) row)
              (set! (-> obj fc-target-slot) slot)
              ;; pc-mb-target-set! cleared the C++ hide/checker/gizmo flags; mirror that here or the
              ;; HUD would claim a state the renderer no longer has.
              (set! (-> obj fc-hide?) #f)
              (set! (-> obj fc-checker?) #f)
              (set! (-> obj fc-gizmos?) #f)
              ;; load that level's index so the name/grade getters and the state dump read THIS row,
              ;; and write the owner's copy-out file (he has no adb).
              (set! (-> obj cur-row) row)
              (pc-mesh-index-load! (if (zero? slot) (-> obj fc-lvl0) (-> obj fc-lvl1)))
              (pc-mesh-index-level! (-> obj level-buf))
              (pc-mesh-browser-export! row))))))))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-enter-freecam ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Enter FREECAM from anywhere: closed (R3 in gameplay), the list screens, or OBSERVE. The camera
   CONTINUES from wherever the engine's camera is right now — pose copied, yaw/pitch derived from
   the current look direction — so entry is seamless. A visible snap on entry is a FAIL."
  (let ((from-observe? (= (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode observe))))
    ;; from fully closed we must first borrow the world (freeze Jak, snapshot the want list...),
    ;; exactly as the list entry does — one shared borrow, one shared give-back (close).
    (when (= (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode closed))
      (mesh-browser-borrow-world obj))
    ;; continue from the RENDERER'S camera pose, i.e. what is on screen this frame.
    (set! (-> obj fc-pos quad) (-> *math-camera* trans quad))
    ;; yaw/pitch from the current look direction. From OBSERVE both ends of the look ray are known
    ;; exactly (camera -> centroid); anywhere else, take the camera rotation basis the engine itself
    ;; uses for "in front of the camera": inv-camera-rot row 2 is the world-space forward
    ;; (position-in-front-of-camera!, engine/camera/cam-interface.gc:13 — and our own OBSERVE matrix
    ;; is copied verbatim into inv-camera-rot by cam-update.gc:325, same convention, same sign).
    (let ((fwd (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
      (cond
        (from-observe?
         (vector-! fwd (-> obj obs-focus) (-> *math-camera* trans))
         (vector-normalize! fwd 1.0))
        (else
         (set! (-> fwd quad) (-> *math-camera* inv-camera-rot vector 2 quad))))
      ;; a degenerate forward (camera exactly on the centroid) would NaN the angles; look north.
      (when (< (vector-length fwd) 0.001)
        (set-vector! fwd 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.0))
      ;; UNITS: atan2-rad (engine/math/trigonometry.gc:829) returns RADIANS in [-pi,pi] directly;
      ;; asin (trigonometry.gc:1065) returns ROTATION UNITS (65536/turn per its docstring), so
      ;; divide by 10430.378 = 65536/2pi (the same constant the light spin uses in reverse).
      (set! (-> obj fc-yaw) (mb-wrap (atan2-rad (-> fwd x) (-> fwd z)) 6.2832))
      (set! (-> obj fc-pitch)
            (fmax MB_EL_MIN (fmin MB_EL_MAX (/ (asin (-> fwd y)) 10430.378)))))
    ;; entering from OBSERVE = the owner was already looking at a mesh: keep it, pre-targeted, so
    ;; the freecam opens with the gizmo/hide/checker toggles immediately live on that mesh.
    (cond
      (from-observe?
       (if (-> obj browse-level)
           (format (clear (-> obj fc-lvl0)) "~A" (-> obj browse-level))
           (format (clear (-> obj fc-lvl0)) ""))
       (if (and (-> obj home-level) (!= (-> obj home-level) (-> obj browse-level)))
           (format (clear (-> obj fc-lvl1)) "~A" (-> obj home-level))
           (format (clear (-> obj fc-lvl1)) ""))
       (pc-mb-pick-levels! (-> obj fc-lvl0) (-> obj fc-lvl1))
       (set! (-> obj fc-target) (-> obj cur-row))
       (set! (-> obj fc-target-slot) 0)
       (pc-mb-target-set! (-> obj cur-row) 0))
      (else
       (set! (-> obj fc-target) -1)))
    ;; C++ cleared its flags on target-set/none — mirror.
    (set! (-> obj fc-hide?) #f)
    (set! (-> obj fc-checker?) #f)
    (set! (-> obj fc-gizmos?) #f)
    (set! (-> obj fc-pick-n) 0)
    (set! (-> obj fc-pick-wait) 0)  ;; V2.1: drop any pick left in flight across an entry
    (set! (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode freecam))
    (set! (-> obj drag) (mesh-browser-drag none))
    ;; MODE 2: the overlay KEEPS the virtual pad live (the freecam is stick-flown; raw-touch mode 1
    ;; would take the owner's only sticks away) and shows its freecam button as active.
    (pc-mb-set-active! 2))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-input-freecam ((obj mesh-browser))
  ;; AXIS CONVENTION (v2.1, owner: strafe + pan were mirrored). Ground truth from the engine, not
  ;; guessed: forward-down->inv-matrix (engine/geometry/geometry.gc:255) builds row0 = fwd x down,
  ;; and the projection's X scale is NEGATIVE (math-camera.gc:142 — the mirror cheat flips it to
  ;; mirror the whole game), so row0 = (cos yaw, 0, -(sin yaw)) points to the screen's LEFT.
  ;; SCREEN-RIGHT for fwd=(sin yaw, 0, cos yaw) is (-(cos yaw), 0, sin yaw), and turning the VIEW
  ;; right means yaw DECREASES — exactly the sign cam-eye uses (cam-states.gc:287-319: stick right
  ;; -> negative angle about local-down). V1 treated row0 as screen-right; that single handedness
  ;; error mirrored both the strafe and the pan.
  ;; LOOK: right stick, same *cpad-list* reads + 24.0 deadzone as OBSERVE. Stick right = view turns
  ;; right (yaw decreases, cam-eye polarity). Stick up = look up (righty decreases upward, so
  ;; subtracting ry raises the pitch — cam-eye's own vertical polarity, verified, left untouched).
  ;; V2.1: complete any in-flight reticle pick (triangle results land a frame or two after R1).
  (mesh-browser-freecam-pick-poll obj)
  (let ((rx (- (the float (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 rightx)) 128.0))
        (ry (- (the float (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 righty)) 128.0)))
    (when (> (fabs rx) 24.0)
      (set! (-> obj fc-yaw) (mb-wrap (- (-> obj fc-yaw) (* rx 0.0009)) 6.2832)))
    (when (> (fabs ry) 24.0)
      (set! (-> obj fc-pitch)
            (fmax MB_EL_MIN (fmin MB_EL_MAX (- (-> obj fc-pitch) (* ry 0.0007)))))))
  ;; FLY: left stick. FULL 3D along the look vector — pushing forward while looking up FLIES UP
  ;; (owner: "left stick to move in all directions including air"). X held = 4x boost.
  (let ((lx (- (the float (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 leftx)) 128.0))
        (ly (- (the float (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 lefty)) 128.0)))
    (when (or (> (fabs lx) 24.0) (> (fabs ly) 24.0))
      (let ((fwd (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
            (rgt (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
            (spd (if (cpad-hold? 0 x) 4096.0 1024.0))  ;; GOAL units/frame at full deflection
            (lxn (if (> (fabs lx) 24.0) (/ lx 128.0) 0.0))
            (lyn (if (> (fabs ly) 24.0) (/ ly 128.0) 0.0)))
        (mesh-browser-freecam-fwd obj fwd)
        ;; rgt = SCREEN-RIGHT = -(fwd x down) — see the axis-convention note at the top of this
        ;; defun. V1 used row0 itself here, which strafed left under a right push.
        (let ((yw (mb-pi-wrap (-> obj fc-yaw))))
          (set-vector! rgt (- (cos-rad yw)) 0.0 (sin-rad yw) 0.0))
        ;; lefty decreases when pushed forward, so forward = -lyn along the look vector.
        (vector+float*! (-> obj fc-pos) (-> obj fc-pos) fwd (* (- lyn) spd))
        (vector+float*! (-> obj fc-pos) (-> obj fc-pos) rgt (* lxn spd)))))
  ;; BUTTONS. The toggles are inert without a target (Triangle defocused them on purpose).
  (cond
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 r1) (mesh-browser-freecam-pick obj 1))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 r2) (mesh-browser-freecam-pick obj -1))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 l1)
     (when (>= (-> obj fc-target) 0)
       (pc-mb-hide-set! 1)
       (set! (-> obj fc-hide?) #t)))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 l2)
     (when (>= (-> obj fc-target) 0)
       (pc-mb-hide-set! 0)
       (set! (-> obj fc-hide?) #f)))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 square)
     (when (>= (-> obj fc-target) 0)
       (set! (-> obj fc-checker?) (not (-> obj fc-checker?)))
       (pc-mb-checker-set! (if (-> obj fc-checker?) 1 0))))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 circle)
     (when (>= (-> obj fc-target) 0)
       (set! (-> obj fc-gizmos?) (not (-> obj fc-gizmos?)))
       (pc-mb-gizmos-set! (if (-> obj fc-gizmos?) 1 0))))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 l3)
     ;; V2.3 MARK / V2.4 UNMARK toggle: flag the polygon under the reticle, or unflag it when it
     ;; is already marked (gizmos must be up — the hover highlight is what the owner is aiming
     ;; with). -1 = nothing hovered: keep the previous count.
     (when (and (>= (-> obj fc-target) 0) (-> obj fc-gizmos?))
       (let ((n (pc-mb-mark-poly!)))
         (when (>= n 0)
           (set! (-> obj fc-marks) n)))))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 triangle)
     ;; DEFOCUS: drop the target; the three toggles become inert (owner's spec).
     (pc-mb-target-clear!)
     (set! (-> obj fc-target) -1)
     (set! (-> obj fc-hide?) #f)
     (set! (-> obj fc-checker?) #f)
     (set! (-> obj fc-gizmos?) #f))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 left) (mesh-browser-bump-tod obj -1.0))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 right) (mesh-browser-bump-tod obj 1.0))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 up) (mesh-browser-bump-relief obj 0.25))
    ((cpad-pressed? 0 down) (mesh-browser-bump-relief obj -0.25)))
  ;; CAMERA: same look-through-other channel as OBSERVE, re-armed every frame.
  (let ((fwd (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (dwn (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
    (mesh-browser-freecam-fwd obj fwd)
    (set-vector! dwn 0.0 -1.0 0.0 0.0)
    (forward-down->inv-matrix *camera-other-matrix* fwd dwn)
    (set! (-> *camera-other-trans* quad) (-> obj fc-pos quad))
    (set! *camera-look-through-other* 2)
    ;; V2.3 HOVER RAY: publish the reticle ray every freecam frame (same origin+fwd the camera and
    ;; the R1 pick use, so the highlighted polygon IS the one under the crosshair by construction).
    ;; on=1 only while a target is set AND its gizmos are up; the browser-close path sends the
    ;; disarming on=0, so this is never called outside the freecam (zero cost when closed).
    (pc-mb-hover-ray! (-> obj fc-pos) fwd
                      (if (and (>= (-> obj fc-target) 0) (-> obj fc-gizmos?)) 1 0)))
  ;; every frame, not just on entry: a title attract cycle can spawn a FRESH othercam mid-flight
  (mesh-browser-set-othercam-sleep #t)
  ;; hold the chosen hour (re-asserted every frame, or the day/night cycle ticks it forward)
  (when (and *mb-tod-hold?* *time-of-day-proc*)
    (set-time-of-day *mb-tod-hour*))
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-draw-freecam ((obj mesh-browser) (buf dma-buffer))
  ;; NO full-screen backdrop: the world must stay fully visible — the freecam IS the viewport.
  ;; RETICLE at screen centre: two thin crossing bars.
  (mesh-browser-rect buf 0.480 0.4975 0.520 0.5025 (new 'static 'rgba :r #xff :g #xff :b #xff :a #xa0))
  (mesh-browser-rect buf 0.4975 0.475 0.5025 0.525 (new 'static 'rgba :r #xff :g #xff :b #xff :a #xa0))
  (mesh-browser-text buf
    "FREECAM  R1/R2 TARGET  L1 HIDE L2 SHOW  SQUARE CHECKER  CIRCLE GIZMOS  TRIANGLE DEFOCUS  R3 EXIT"
    0.02 0.045 (font-color green))
  (cond
    ((>= (-> obj fc-target) 0)
     (let ((raw (-> obj cur-row)))
       (pc-mesh-index-name! raw (-> obj name-buf))
       ;; the identifier the owner quotes back — exactly the OBSERVE style, via the dedicated
       ;; buffers (mb-grade-string writes grade-buf, NOT the shared *temp-string* the outer
       ;; string-format formats into — the clobber trap documented at grade-buf).
       (mesh-browser-text buf
         (string-format "TARGET ~S / ~S  ~S  SHELL ~D  TEX ~D"
                        (-> obj level-buf) (-> obj name-buf)
                        (if (= (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_SYSTEM) 1) "TIE" "TFRAG")
                        (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_SHELL) (pc-mesh-index-geti raw MB_GI_TEX))
         0.02 0.095 (font-color white))
       (mesh-browser-text buf
         (string-format "GRADE A_SIGN=~S  (files/mesh_select.txt)" (mb-grade-string obj raw))
         0.02 0.145 (font-color yellow))
       ;; DRAWS = the target's SUBMITTED draw count last frame, straight from the renderer
       ;; (pc-mb-rt-geti 4). The owner-facing dead-target tell: DRAWS 0 while un-hidden means
       ;; "this row has nothing on screen here — cycle R1", the silent state v2.1 was reopened on.
       (mesh-browser-text buf
         (string-format "HIDE=~D CHECKER=~D GIZMOS=~D  PICKS=~D  DRAWS ~D"
                        (if (-> obj fc-hide?) 1 0)
                        (if (-> obj fc-checker?) 1 0)
                        (if (-> obj fc-gizmos?) 1 0)
                        (-> obj fc-pick-n)
                        (pc-mb-rt-geti 4))
         0.02 0.195 (font-color cyan))
       ;; V2.3: reticle-hover + mark HUD, only while the gizmos (and their wireframe) are up —
       ;; that is when a polygon can be hovered/marked at all. Phone-readable short lines.
       (when (-> obj fc-gizmos?)
         (let ((hov (pc-mb-rt-geti 12)))
           (if (>= hov 0)
               (mesh-browser-text buf (string-format "TRI ~D" hov) 0.02 0.245 (font-color white))
               (mesh-browser-text buf "TRI -" 0.02 0.245 (font-color white))))
         (mesh-browser-text buf
           (string-format "MARKS ~D -> mesh_marks.jsonl" (-> obj fc-marks))
           0.02 0.295 (font-color yellow))
         ;; control hint, same green style as the top hint line
         (mesh-browser-text buf "L3/MARK: flag polygon" 0.02 0.345 (font-color green)))))
    (else
     (mesh-browser-text buf "NO TARGET - AIM THE RETICLE, PRESS R1" 0.02 0.095 (font-color yellow))))
  (none))

;; ---- observable-state dump -------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; files/mesh_browser_state.txt. Two jobs: it is the owner's copy-out of the identifier he is looking
;; at (he has no adb), and it is what makes the touch claim FALSIFIABLE — inject a gesture, read the
;; file, and the browser's state either moved or it did not. Written only while the browser is open,
;; and only when something actually changed.

(defun mb-mode-name ((m mesh-browser-mode))
  (case m
    (((mesh-browser-mode levels)) "LEVELS")
    (((mesh-browser-mode list)) "LIST")
    (((mesh-browser-mode observe)) "OBSERVE")
    (((mesh-browser-mode freecam)) "FREECAM")
    (else "CLOSED")))

(defun mesh-browser-state-sig ((obj mesh-browser))
  (let ((s 0))
    (+! s (* 1000003 (the int (-> obj mode))))
    (+! s (* 7919 (the int (-> obj filter))))
    (+! s (* 131 (-> obj sel)))
    (+! s (* 1009 (-> obj cur-row)))
    (+! s (* 53 (-> obj level-index)))
    (+! s (the int (-> obj scroll-f)))
    (+! s (* 17 (the int (* 100.0 (-> obj obs-az)))))
    (+! s (* 19 (the int (* 100.0 (-> obj obs-el)))))
    (+! s (* 23 (the int (* 0.01 (-> obj obs-dist)))))
    (+! s (* 29 (the int (* 100.0 (-> obj spin)))))
    (+! s (* 31 (if (-> obj checker?) 1 0)))
    (+! s (* 37 (-> *pc-settings* pbr-displacement)))
    (+! s (* 41 (the int (* 100.0 (-> *pc-settings* pbr-texture-relief)))))
    (+! s (* 43 (the int (* 10.0 *mb-tod-hour*))))
    ;; FREECAM: every fly step (decimetre-resolution position), look, retarget and toggle must move
    ;; the signature so it dumps within 8 frames. The rt counters are deliberately NOT in the sig —
    ;; they advance every rendered frame; the 180-frame heartbeat carries their progress.
    (+! s (* 47 (the int (* 10.0 (* MB_M (-> obj fc-pos x))))))
    (+! s (* 59 (the int (* 10.0 (* MB_M (-> obj fc-pos z))))))
    (+! s (* 61 (the int (* 100.0 (-> obj fc-yaw)))))
    (+! s (* 67 (the int (* 100.0 (-> obj fc-pitch)))))
    (+! s (* 71 (-> obj fc-target)))
    (+! s (* 73 (if (-> obj fc-hide?) 1 0)))
    (+! s (* 79 (if (-> obj fc-checker?) 1 0)))
    (+! s (* 83 (if (-> obj fc-gizmos?) 1 0)))
    ;; V2.3: a MARK must trigger a dump (marks= is the mark's evidence line). The HOVER ordinal is
    ;; deliberately NOT in the sig — it changes every frame the reticle moves and would spam dumps;
    ;; the gizmos flag (its gate) is already folded in at *83 above.
    (+! s (* 89 (-> obj fc-marks)))
    s))

(defun mesh-browser-dump-state ((obj mesh-browser))
  (pc-mb-state-begin!)
  (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "MBSTATE 2 mode=~S level=~S filter=~S"
          (mb-mode-name (-> obj mode)) (-> obj level-buf) (mb-filter-name (-> obj filter)))
  (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
  (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "n_filtered=~D n_total=~D scroll=~D sel=~D row=~D"
          (-> obj n-filtered) (-> obj n-total) (the int (-> obj scroll-f)) (-> obj sel) (-> obj cur-row))
  (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
  ;; NOT in the LEVEL PICKER: there n-filtered is the LEVEL count and `view` still holds the previous
  ;; level's row map, so this block would republish the PREVIOUS mesh's material and centroid. A
  ;; harness sampling the file between two selections would then read an unchanged focus= — the very
  ;; "always the same spot" signature this evidence exists to detect. Emit it only where it is real.
  ;; In FREECAM the target came from the reticle, not the list, so view/sel are stale — read cur-row
  ;; directly, and only while something IS targeted; the LEVELS/LIST/OBSERVE path is unchanged.
  (let ((mraw -1))
    (cond
      ((= (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode freecam))
       (when (>= (-> obj fc-target) 0) (set! mraw (-> obj cur-row))))
      ((and (> (-> obj n-filtered) 0) (!= (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode levels)))
       (set! mraw (-> obj view (min (-> obj sel) (+ (-> obj n-filtered) -1))))))
    (when (>= mraw 0)
      (pc-mesh-index-name! mraw (-> obj name-buf))
      (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "material=~S system=~S shell=~D tex=~D grade=~S"
              (-> obj name-buf)
              (if (= (pc-mesh-index-geti mraw MB_GI_SYSTEM) 1) "TIE" "TFRAG")
              (pc-mesh-index-geti mraw MB_GI_SHELL) (pc-mesh-index-geti mraw MB_GI_TEX)
              (mb-grade-string obj mraw))
      (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))))
  ;; cam_dist in METRES, same unit as cam_r/focus/cam below: the harness asserts cam_r == cam_dist
  ;; to prove the camera sits on the orbit sphere, and a GOAL-units cam_dist next to a metres cam_r
  ;; makes that comparison fail by construction (4096x apart).
  (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "cam_az=~f cam_el=~f cam_dist=~f spin=~f"
          (-> obj obs-az) (-> obj obs-el) (* MB_M (-> obj obs-dist)) (-> obj spin))
  (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
  ;; ---- FREE-CAMERA EVIDENCE, all in METRES ------------------------------------------------------
  ;; focus  = this mesh's centroid, straight out of the index; it IS the orbit origin.
  ;; cam    = where the engine's camera actually ended up ((-> *math-camera* trans), i.e. what the
  ;;          renderer used, not what we intended).
  ;; cam_r  = |cam - focus|. If the camera really orbits THIS centroid, cam_r == cam_dist. Two meshes
  ;;          with different centroids therefore cannot report the same cam — which is precisely the
  ;;          "warp toujours au meme endroit" claim, made falsifiable.
  ;; (GOAL caps a call at 8 arguments, so this is spread over several short lines.)
  ;; Only in OBSERVE: outside it there is no mesh under the camera and publishing a stale focus=
  ;; would be worse than publishing nothing.
  (when (= (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode observe))
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "focus=~f,~f,~f"
            (* MB_M (-> obj obs-focus x)) (* MB_M (-> obj obs-focus y)) (* MB_M (-> obj obs-focus z)))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "cam=~f,~f,~f cam_r=~f"
            (* MB_M (-> *math-camera* trans x)) (* MB_M (-> *math-camera* trans y))
            (* MB_M (-> *math-camera* trans z))
            (* MB_M (vector-vector-distance (-> *math-camera* trans) (-> obj obs-focus))))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
    ;; the look-through channel itself, so a harness can tell "our write lost the channel" (other=
    ;; wrong / lto=0) from "math-camera was overwritten after cam-update applied it" (other= right,
    ;; lto>0, cam= elsewhere). This is what pinned the title-screen camera fight.
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "lto=~D other=~f,~f,~f"
            *camera-look-through-other*
            (* MB_M (-> *camera-other-trans* x)) (* MB_M (-> *camera-other-trans* y))
            (* MB_M (-> *camera-other-trans* z)))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf)))
  ;; ---- FREECAM EVIDENCE (metres/radians) --------------------------------------------------------
  ;; fc/yaw/pitch make every fly step falsifiable; target/hide/checker2/gizmos are the GOAL-side
  ;; toggle state; the rt_* lines are the RENDER-THREAD counters (pc-mb-rt-geti) — the proof that a
  ;; toggle actually changed what is DRAWN, not just a flag in this file (the V1 sin of the two dead
  ;; toggles: state moved, pixels did not).
  (when (= (-> obj mode) (mesh-browser-mode freecam))
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "fc=~f,~f,~f yaw=~f pitch=~f"
            (* MB_M (-> obj fc-pos x)) (* MB_M (-> obj fc-pos y)) (* MB_M (-> obj fc-pos z))
            (-> obj fc-yaw) (-> obj fc-pitch))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "target=~D slot=~D hide=~D checker2=~D gizmos=~D pick_n=~D"
            (-> obj fc-target) (-> obj fc-target-slot)
            (if (-> obj fc-hide?) 1 0) (if (-> obj fc-checker?) 1 0)
            (if (-> obj fc-gizmos?) 1 0) (-> obj fc-pick-n))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "rt_hidden=~D rt_checker=~D rt_gizmo_draws=~D rt_gizmo_faces=~D"
            (pc-mb-rt-geti 0) (pc-mb-rt-geti 1) (pc-mb-rt-geti 2) (pc-mb-rt-geti 3))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
    ;; V2.1 PER-FRAME renderer counters (owner: every toggle "dead" while variables flipped — only
    ;; a per-frame count shows the target's submitted draws hitting ZERO when hidden). rtf_target =
    ;; draws SUBMITTED for the target last frame (hide: N>0 -> 0 -> N>0), rtf_checker = checker
    ;; binds last frame, rtf_gizmo = gizmo line prims last frame, rtf_relief = the relief factor
    ;; (x100) the PBR shader uniforms were actually pushed with last frame.
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "rtf_target=~D rtf_checker=~D rtf_gizmo=~D rtf_relief=~D"
            (pc-mb-rt-geti 4) (pc-mb-rt-geti 5) (pc-mb-rt-geti 6) (pc-mb-rt-geti 7))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
    ;; V2.2 renderer counters: rtf_cfull = FULL checker-set binds (normal+rough+height) on the
    ;; target's draws last frame (Square must engage the whole debug material, not the albedo
    ;; alone); rtf_tess = target draws submitted on the TESS program last frame (the displacement
    ;; path actually TAKEN); rtf_gizmo_px = framebuffer pixels the gizmo pass CHANGED last frame
    ;; (readback proof: emitted-but-invisible cannot pass this).
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "rtf_cfull=~D rtf_tess=~D rtf_gizmo_px=~D"
            (pc-mb-rt-geti 8) (pc-mb-rt-geti 9) (pc-mb-rt-geti 10))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
    ;; V2.3 renderer counters: rtf_wire = WIREFRAME edges drawn last frame (>0 while gizmos on,
    ;; 0 off), hover = hovered triangle ordinal under the reticle (-1 none), marks = the GOAL-side
    ;; ACTIVE mark count (V2.4: unmark decrements; the C++ count is pc-mb-rt-geti 13).
    ;; V2.4 renderer counters: rtf_marked = marked triangles DRAWN by the persistent-highlight
    ;; pass last frame (proof: == marks while the browser is open), rtf_occ = depth-test samples
    ;; PASSED in the gizmo visible sub-pass last frame (occlusion query: falls when the target
    ;; is behind interposed geometry).
    (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "rtf_wire=~D hover=~D marks=~D rtf_marked=~D rtf_occ=~D"
            (pc-mb-rt-geti 11) (pc-mb-rt-geti 12) (-> obj fc-marks)
            (pc-mb-rt-geti 14) (pc-mb-rt-geti 15))
    (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
    ;; V2.2 pick-candidate export, for the harness occlusion/frustum cases: the surviving
    ;; candidates of the LAST pick, in rank order, as row:slot:surface-distance-cm. An occluded
    ;; mesh B behind A on the same ray must appear here AFTER A (never as the target); a mesh
    ;; behind the camera must never appear at all.
    (let ((n (min 6 (-> obj fc-pick-n))))
      (clear (-> obj line-buf))
      (format (-> obj line-buf) "pickc=")
      (dotimes (i n)
        (format (-> obj line-buf) "~D:~D:~D|"
                (pc-mb-pick-geti i MB_PK_ROW) (pc-mb-pick-geti i MB_PK_SLOT)
                (pc-mb-pick-geti i MB_PK_TCM)))
      (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))))
  ;; player_moved = how far the PLAYER has travelled since the browser opened. The owner's whole
  ;; correction is that this must stay 0: the camera goes to the mesh, Jak does not.
  (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "player=~f,~f,~f player_moved=~f"
          (if *target* (* MB_M (-> *target* root trans x)) 0.0)
          (if *target* (* MB_M (-> *target* root trans y)) 0.0)
          (if *target* (* MB_M (-> *target* root trans z)) 0.0)
          (if *target* (* MB_M (vector-vector-distance (-> *target* root trans) (-> obj home-pos))) 0.0))
  (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
  (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "frozen=~D home_level=~A browse_level=~A lvl_status=~A"
          (if (-> obj frozen?) 1 0)
          (-> obj home-level)
          (-> obj browse-level)
          (if (-> obj browse-level) (level-status *level* (-> obj browse-level)) 'none))
  (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
  (if *mb-tod-hold?*
      (format (clear (-> obj sub-buf)) "~f" *mb-tod-hour*)
      (format (clear (-> obj sub-buf)) "CYCLE"))
  (format (clear (-> obj line-buf)) "checker=~D disp=~S relief=~f tod=~S"
          (if (-> obj checker?) 1 0) (mb-disp-name) (-> *pc-settings* pbr-texture-relief) (-> obj sub-buf))
  (pc-mb-state-line! (-> obj line-buf))
  (pc-mb-state-end!)
  (none))

(defun mesh-browser-maybe-dump ((obj mesh-browser))
  "Write the state file when something changed, but never more than once every 8 frames: during a
   scroll or an orbit the signature changes EVERY frame, and a 60 Hz file write would stutter the
   very frame rate the owner is meant to be judging. A heartbeat every 3 s keeps the file fresh
   even when nothing moves."
  (+! (-> obj dump-timer) 1)
  (let ((sig (mesh-browser-state-sig obj)))
    (when (or (and (!= sig (-> obj dump-sig)) (>= (-> obj dump-timer) 8))
              (>= (-> obj dump-timer) 180))
      (set! (-> obj dump-sig) sig)
      (set! (-> obj dump-timer) 0)
      (mesh-browser-dump-state obj)))
  (none))

;; ---- the single per-frame entry point -------------------------------------------------------------
;; Hooked into (update *pc-settings*) right after draw-pc-fps-counter. Does NOTHING while closed, so
;; the normal render path is byte-for-byte unchanged when the browser is off.

(defun mesh-browser-update ()
  ;; R3 in plain gameplay = jump straight into the FREECAM (the owner's reticle-first entry; the
  ;; overlay's freecam button injects exactly this press). This single pad test is the ONLY thing
  ;; the closed browser does per frame — the normal path stays byte-for-byte unchanged otherwise.
  (when (not (mesh-browser-active?))
    (when (and (= *master-mode* 'game) (cpad-pressed? 0 r3))
      (cpad-clear! 0 r3)
      (mesh-browser-enter-freecam *mesh-browser*)))
  (when (mesh-browser-active?)
    (mesh-browser-poll-touch)
    ;; central R3, before the mode dispatch: from any list screen it ENTERS the freecam; from the
    ;; freecam it fully CLOSES the browser (world restored — going back to the list is via the menu).
    (when (cpad-pressed? 0 r3)
      (cpad-clear! 0 r3)
      (if (= (-> *mesh-browser* mode) (mesh-browser-mode freecam))
          (mesh-browser-close *mesh-browser*)
          (mesh-browser-enter-freecam *mesh-browser*)))
    ;; input first (may change mode), then draw the current mode.
    (case (-> *mesh-browser* mode)
      (((mesh-browser-mode levels)) (mesh-browser-input-levels *mesh-browser*))
      (((mesh-browser-mode list)) (mesh-browser-input-list *mesh-browser*))
      (((mesh-browser-mode observe)) (mesh-browser-input-observe *mesh-browser*))
      (((mesh-browser-mode freecam)) (mesh-browser-input-freecam *mesh-browser*)))
    (when (mesh-browser-active?)
      ;; The browser has now consumed this frame's pad. Blank the buttons so the same press does not
      ;; ALSO reach the game underneath (START would pull the progress menu up over the browser).
      ;; This runs after service-cpads and before the next process pass (engine/game/main.gc:568),
      ;; and it is undone by the next service-cpads, so nothing persists once the browser closes.
      ;; The FREECAM needs this blanking just as much: Jak is asleep, but the progress menu would
      ;; still pop on START if the game saw the browser's buttons.
      (set! (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 button0-abs 0) (pad-buttons))
      (set! (-> *cpad-list* cpads 0 button0-rel 0) (pad-buttons))
      (mesh-browser-maybe-dump *mesh-browser*)
      ;; draw into the always-live debug bucket (renders on x86 GL and Android GLES).
      (with-dma-buffer-add-bucket ((buf (-> (current-frame) global-buf)) (bucket-id debug-no-zbuf))
        (case (-> *mesh-browser* mode)
          (((mesh-browser-mode levels)) (mesh-browser-draw-levels *mesh-browser* buf))
          (((mesh-browser-mode list)) (mesh-browser-draw-list *mesh-browser* buf))
          (((mesh-browser-mode observe)) (mesh-browser-draw-observe *mesh-browser* buf))
          (((mesh-browser-mode freecam)) (mesh-browser-draw-freecam *mesh-browser* buf))))))
  (none))
